\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Leu jumps from six-week lows, bond yields rise at auctions\b0\par\par\uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 16:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Leu gains; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par     * Romanian government may alter new taxes\par     * Hungary, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Romania\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sell bonds at increased yields\par     * Forint hits 10-month high, British Brexit vote watched\par \par  (Adds government bond auctions in Bucharest and Budapest)\par     By Sandor Peto and Luiza Ilie\par     BUDAPEST/BUCHAREST, March 14 (Reuters) - The leu\par rebounded on Thursday from the six-week low it reached late on\par Wednesday, after what market participants said may have been\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Romania\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Romanian government bond yields rose to multi-week highs and\par the finance ministry sold five-year bonds at an average yield of\par 4.47 percent, up 18 basis points from a sale four weeks ago.\par       \par     Romanian asset prices have been jittery in the three months\par since the government announced new taxes on various businesses,\par including banks.\par     The government is expected to work out changes to the levies\par by next week to prevent a downgrade of its credit rating outlook\par to negative from stable by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The leu gained 0.3 percent against the euro to\par trade at 4.768 at 0930 GMT, off Wednesday's six-week lows at\par 4.78. \par     "The historically high turnover (on Wednesday) is supporting\par the idea of official offers coming in to protect the Romanian\par leu," Bucharest-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a note.\par     Romania's overnight ROBOR interbank interest rate\par  was bid at 1.41 percent, unchanged from Wednesday\par and still near three-month lows.\par     The yield on the five-year benchmark Romanian bond\par  was bid higher by 7 basis points in the secondary\par market at 4.32 percent.\par     Government bond yields rose 1 to 2 basis points in the\par region's main markets, tracking Bunds.\par     The Hungarian government sold 106 billion forints ($381.08\par million) worth of bonds at its bi-weekly auction and top-up\par tender, boosting its original 65 billion forint offer.\par  \par     Yields rose from an auction held two weeks ago. But after\par the sale they retreated by about 1 basis point in the secondary\par market, indicating that demand remained strong.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed as investors waited for a\par third British parliamentary vote this week on its planned exit\par from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , this time on whether to delay the March\par 29 deadline.  \par     The forint gained 0.2 percent against the euro to\par 314.32, setting a 10-month high amid expectations the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will start to tighten policy at its meeting on\par March 26.\par     Poland's zloty weakened, trading at 4.3045 versus\par the euro. \par     In equities markets, the stocks OTP, the region's\par biggest independent lender which reported record earnings for\par 2018 two weeks ago, rose more than 1 percent to a record high.  \par   \par             CEE       SNAPSHOT   AT                         \par             MARKETS             1459 CET            \par                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCI\f28 \b0 \hig