\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Leu jumps from 6-week lows, tax debate stays in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Leu firms, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -dealers\par     * Investors watch how Romanian government will alter new\par taxes\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mixed, British Brexit vote watched closely\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sometimes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , its chief says\par \par     By Sandor Peto and Luiza Ilie\par     BUDAPEST/BUCHAREST, March 14 (Reuters) - The leu\par jumped on Thursday, rebounding from 6-week lows set late in the\par previous session, in what market participants said was possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Romania\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Romanian asset prices has been jittery in the past three\par months since the government announced new taxes on various\par business sectors including banks.\par     The government is expected to work out changes to the levies\par by next week to prevent a downgrade of its credit rating outlook\par to negative from stable by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The leu firmed a quarter of a percent against the\par euro through the 4.77 psychological line, to trade at 4.768 at\par 0930 GMT, off Wednesday's 6-week lows at 4.78. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a track record of managing the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market sometimes. One Bucharest-based dealer\par said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was probably behind the leu's rebound.\par     "The historically high turnover (on Wednesday) is supporting\par the idea of official offers coming in to protect the Romanian\par leu," Bucharest-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a note.\par     Romania's overnight ROBOR interbank interest rate\par  was bid at 1.41 percent, unchanged from Wednesday\par and still near 3-month lows.\par     Given the uncertainty over S&P's rating, an auction of\par 5-year Romanian bonds on Thursday "seems to have come at the\par wrong time", but the government could sell the full amount if it\par allows some rise in the yield, the ING note added.\par     The yield on the 5-year benchmark Romanian bond\par was bid higher by 8 basis points in the secondary market to 4.33\par percent.\par     Hungarian yields rose 2-3 basis points ahead of the\par government's auction on Thursday as the market digests a rise in\par the sale at the bi-weekly auctions to above 100 billion forints \par ($359.69 million), one trader said.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed as investors were looking at\par the impact of the third British parliamentary vote this week\par concerning its planned exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , this time\par on whether to delay the March 29 deadline.  \par     The forint firmed slightly, trading near\par Wednesday's 10-month highs amid expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will start to tighten policy at its meeting on\par March 26.\par     Poland's zloty eased a touch, but remained stuck\par at the 4.3 psychological line versus the euro.\par     Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Adam Glapinski said the bank\par has sometimes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market but\par these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been limited.\par     DM TMS Brokers analyst Konrad Bialas said the stability of\par Poland's economy and monetary policy had kept the zloty very\par stable in the past months, rather than \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \par     \par             CEE       SNAPSHOT   AT                         \par             MARKETS             1030 CET            \par                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCI\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                               \par                       ES                            \par                       Latest    Previous  Daily     Change\par                       bid       close     change    in 2019\par  Czech      <EURCZK=   25.6670   25.6520    -0.06%    +0.16%\par  crown      >                                       \par  Hungary    <EURHUF=  314.5000  314.8500    +0.11%    +2.09%\par  forint     >                                       \par  Polish     <EURPLN=    4.3020    4.3005    -0.03%    -0.29%\par  zloty      >                                       \par  Romanian   <EURRON=    4.7680    4.7799    +0.25%    -2.39%\par  leu        >                                       \par  Croatian   <EURHRK=    7.4195    7.4163    -0.04%    -0.13%\par  kuna       >                                       \par  Serbian    <EURRSD=  118.0500  118.1900    +0.12%    +0.21%\par  dinar      >                                       \par  Note:      calculated from               1800 CET          \par  daily                                              \par  change                                             \par                          