\par\par \b \uc2 Poland, Romania Likely to Keep Rates on Hold -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2018\par 10:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0807 GMT - Poland and Romania decide on Wednesday whether to raise interest rates or not. \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says both will likely remain on hold, with the \uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  holding the rate at 1.5%, likely throughout 2019, and \uc2 National Bank of Romania\uc2  keeping the rate at 2.5%. \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to raise rates "for as long as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's deposit rate remains negative, and as long as inflation stays within the 1.5-3.5% target range." \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable to ensure inflation moderates." EUR/PLN is down 0.2% at 4.2890 and EUR/RON is flat at 4.6664. Both decisions are due later in the day. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0805 GMT - \uc2 Aston Martin\uc2  bond yields fall after shares in the luxury-car maker were priced at GDP19 per share at its initial public offering on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange\uc2  , valuing the firm at GBP4.33 billion. Yields on \uc2 Aston Martin\uc2  's 5.75% April 2022 sterling-denominated bonds fall as low as 4.93% from 4.967% in early trading, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . "Today's listing on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange\uc2  represents a historic milestone for \uc2 Aston Martin Lagonda\uc2  . We are delighted by the positive response we have received from investors across the world and are very pleased to welcome our new shareholders to the register," chief executive Andy Palmer said.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0753 GMT - The Turkish lira falls after data showed annual Turkish inflation jumped to 24.52% in September from 17.90% in August, lifting USD/TRY to a five-day high of 6.0912. A higher inflation number often boosts a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it means interest rates will rise, making money more expensive. But in Turkey--whose \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been reluctant in the past to raise rates to curb inflation--there are concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not have raised rates rises sufficiently to prevent inflation running out of control. President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  has previously expressed a preference for lower interest rates. USD/TRY last trades up 1.1% at 6.0514. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0753 GMT - Taiwan's growth momentum is likely to slow after 1H's 3.2% GDP increase, says \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  , with the US-China trade dispute a key concern. The island is heavily dependent on trade, and the 2 countries are among Taiwan's largest markets. That as China is the "preferred offshore manufacturing base" for many Taiwan exporters, the investment bank reminds. It estimates that Taiwan GDP growth would be slashed by 1.8 percentage points in "the worst-case scenario of a full-blown US-China trade war." StanChart has predicted 2.8% GDP growth for all of this year; 2017's increase was 2.9%. (chester.yung@wsj.com; @chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0747 GMT - The Singapore dollar will likely remain under pressure through mid-2019 as "gradual" gains in the greenback is seen continuing, says \uc2 UOB\uc2  in setting a S$1.41 target for then, versus an end-of-2018 call of S$1.39. It add that "given the backdrop of overwhelming US-dollar strength, the risk is that these point forecasts may be reached sooner than later." Meanwhile, the investment bank doesn't see Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening policy further next week amid recent economic reading having "noticeably" weakened of late. The dollar has edged higher this afternoon and is up 0.1% for the day at S$1.3745. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT - \uc2 Telecom Italia\uc2  bond yields fall after it said late Tuesday that it had invested EUR1.69 billion in a block of 5G internet bandwidth as part of Italy's mobile spectrum auction. It also successfully bid EUR33 million for a separate block and has already won bids for two other sections, bringing its total investment in this auction to EUR2.41 billion. Yields on \uc2 Telecom Italia\uc2  's 7.75% January 2033 euro-denominated bond erase early trading gains and fall as low as 4.302% from a peak of 4.373%, according to Tradeweb.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0733 GMT - German 10-year Bund yields trade higher, indicating less investor appetite for safe havens amid the Italian turmoil, but \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  's analysts say that developments in Italy will remain a key driver of Bunds near term. "In the near term its dynamic [that of Bunds] will be driven by how the mood on Italy evolves," says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  . The ongoing weakness of Italian government bonds has fanned strong support for German Bunds in the past few days and other core/semi-core eurozone government bonds. The 10-year Bund yield is trading 2 basis points higher at 0.45%, while the 10-year BTP yield is trading 8 basis points lower at 3.34%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0731 GMT - The euro continues to be driven by the Italian budget projections, this time going up on reports that Italy may not pencil in another 2.4% deficit-to-GDP projection for 2020 and 2021. Against the dollar, the euro rises 0.2% to 1.1577. \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says risks are contained and EUR/USD is somewhat safe from major falls. Only a break below the August lows around 1.13 would trigger a more intense sell-off. "Interestingly, EUR/CHF has so far proved more resilient than expected to increasing pressure on Italian assets, as it has failed to drop below the 1.1350 handle," \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says. EUR/CHF last up 0.3% at 1.1404. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0723 GMT - The Nikkei Singapore PMI fell into contraction territory last month, sliding to 49.6 from August's 51.1, the first sub-50 reading in 2 1/2 years. The survey of the private-sector economy, conducted by \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2  for Nikkei, contrasts with the official \uc2 PMI\uc2  reading released last night, which showed a slight drop to 52.4. In the Nikkei report, it says declines in output and new orders weighed on \uc2 PMI\uc2  while export sales fell further. Singapore manufacturing has been widely expected to slow amid the global trade tensions. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0719 GMT - Standard Chartered trims its 2018 GDP-growth view for Hong Kong to 3.6% from 3.8%--well within the government's 3-4% forecast range--in anticipation of "looming trade challenges and higher interest rates." The investment bank notes the US-China trade fight has yet to affect the city's exports, but does expect that by year's end. Meanwhile, StanChart cuts its 2019 growth forecast to 3% from 3.4% as the expected export slowdown and likelihood of further interest-rate increases cap GDP gains. (chester.yung@wsj.com; @chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0715 GMT - Global trade uncertainty isn't likely to hold back Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from tightening next week, predicts \uc2 OCBC\uc2  unit \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2  . It expects the MAS to "slightly increase" the policy-band slope of the local dollar's nominal effective exchange rate to 1%/year from 0.5%. "The cyclical story in Singapore continues to justify incremental MAS tightening," \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2  adds, with economic growth having been resilient since the last \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting in April. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0658 GMT - When Spain taps its recently launched November 2023 inflation-linked bond on Thursday, that will raise the bond's liquidity to levels that make it eligible for certain indexes, say \uc2 Citi\uc2 's strategists. Everything else equal, this makes the bond more attractive and could thereby broaden its investor base. The auction will take the outstanding amount above EUR2.5 billion, the "eligibility threshold for certain bond indexes like [formerly \uc2 Citi\uc2 ] EuroILSI," they say. Spain will offer EUR250 million to EUR750 million in the linker, along with EUR4 billion to EUR5 billion offer in 2021-, 2028- and 2029-dated conventional bonds. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 03, 2018 04:07 ET (08:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020181003eea3000i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
