\par\par \b \uc2 Poland, Romania Likely to Keep Rates on Hold -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 158 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2018\par 10:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0807 GMT - Poland and Romania decide on Wednesday whether to raise interest rates or not. \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says both will likely remain on hold, with the \uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  holding the rate at 1.5%, likely throughout 2019, and \uc2 National Bank of Romania\uc2  keeping the rate at 2.5%. \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to raise rates "for as long as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deposit rate remains negative, and as long as inflation stays within the 1.5-3.5% target range." \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable to ensure inflation moderates." EUR/PLN is down 0.2% at 4.2890 and EUR/RON is flat at 4.6664. Both decisions are due later in the day. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 03, 2018 04:07 ET (08:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020181003eea3000l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
