\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romania - Factors to watch on Oct 8\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2013\par 08:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds press digest)\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 PROSECUTORS SAY ROMANIAN DEPUTY PM ABUSED POWER IN 2012 VOTE\par \par \uc2 Romanian prosecutors charged Deputy Prime Minister Liviu Dragnea on Monday with orchestrating a campaign of bribery, threats and fraud to try to swing a vote to impeach President Traian Basescu.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA FINAL GDP EXPANDS 1.5 PCT Y/Y IN Q2-STATS\par \par \uc2 Romania's economy grew by 1.5 percent on the year in the second quarter, confirming an earlier estimate, driven by exports and slowly recovering consumption, final official data showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA SELLS 700 MLN LEI IN 1-YEAR T-BILLS\par \par \uc2 Romania sold a planned 700 million lei ($214.97 million) in one-year treasury bills on Monday, with an average accepted yield of 3.52 percent, 36 basis points down from a previous tender on Sept. 16, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA NET WAGE UP 4.6 PCT Y/Y IN AUGUST\par \par \uc2 The average Romanian monthly wage rose 4.6 percent on the year to 1,604 lei ($490) in August, and was down 1.9 percent from the previous month, the National Statistics Board said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA'S 8-MONTH ENERGY OUTPUT FALLS 7.2 PCT Y/Y\par \par \uc2 Romania's energy production fell 7.2 percent on the year in January-August, while imports plunged 22.2 percent, data from the National Statistics Board showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 CEE MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown firmed to a new four-month high on Monday in response to stronger than expected industrial output data that helped to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to levels that raise chances of the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen its rise.\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY MINISTER RESIGNS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Economy Minister Varujan Vosganian resigned on Monday. Prosecutors said Vosganian undermined the national economy. The senate rejected on Monday a request to start his prosecution in the case as Vosganian is also a senator.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 1\par \par \uc2 IT TRANSACTION\par \par \uc2 American investment fund \uc2 Francisco Partners\uc2  bought Romanian IT company \uc2 Avangate\uc2  for an undisclosed amount.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 1\par \par \uc2 CFR MARFA\par \par \uc2 The transport ministry plans to extend to deadline for the privatisation of rail freight carrier \uc2 CFR Marfa\uc2  to Dec. 20 from mid-October. Ziarul Financiar, Page 3\par \par \uc2 For a schedule of forthcoming Romanian events, double click , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt       Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       \par  Romania Market Report       Romanian money      \par  Emerging Market Debt    Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \par  All Emerging Markets news   CEE indicators  \par  All East Europe News         E.Europe equities     \par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   \par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  \par  Romanian indicators        \par  Main page of Reuters poll  \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 ABN | D | RDN | REVU | M | E | RBN | G | RNP | DNP | PTD | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131008e9a800061\par }\