\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Czech crown climbs after decision against  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2013\par 16:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps interest rates on hold\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Governor says likelihood of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains high\par     * Shares in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Romania\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Fondul hit record high on buyback plan\par     BUDAPEST/BUCHAREST, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The Czech crown extended gains\par against the euro on Thursday after a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meeting decided against\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     With Czech interest rates close to zero, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said for\par months that it will consider \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to help lift inflation back to target\par and boost exporters as the economy recovers after edging out of its 18-month\par recession in the second quarter. \par     "We did not launch them (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), however we agreed that the\par probability is not really changing ... and remains high," Czech National Bank\par Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Miroslav Singer\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. \par     By 1345 GMT, the crown was bid at 25.692 per euro, up 0.6 percent\par on the day, extending gains from earlier in the session.\par     "For now, so long as the economy continues to recover and inflation doesn't\par drop sharply, we doubt that a majority of MPC members will vote in favour of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at upcoming meetings," Capital Economics said in a note. \par     "Either way, the bigger picture is that monetary conditions are set to\par remain extremely loose until 2015 at the earliest."\par     Other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were slightly weaker. The Polish zloty \par was down 0.3 percent, while the Hungarian forint and Romanian leu\par  were 0.1 percent weaker.\par     "Risk sentiment is a little off, given the U.S. budget debate," one\par Bucharest trader said.\par     Shares, which have benefited from the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision last\par week to keep its stimulus intact, were mostly stronger, though traders said they\par could face pressure as attention moves to fending off the possibility of a\par damaging debt default. \par     Poland's broad market index led gains with a 1.3 percent advance on\par the day, firming to its highest level in almost six years, supported by rising\par bank shares on expectations of an economic rebound. \par     In Romania, shares in investment fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fondul Proprietatea\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par outperformed the blue chip index and reached a record high a day after\par announcing plans to buy back roughly 4.4 percent of its shares at an estimated\par cost of 441.6 million lei ($133.2 million). \par    \par                CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 1559 CET\par  ************************** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ************************\par                              Latest  Previous   Daily   Change\par                              bid     close      change  in 2013\par  Czech crown                 25.679    25.849  +0.66%  -2.46%\par  Hungarian forint           299.400   299.140   -0.09%  -2.82%\par  Polish zloty                 4.229     4.216    -0.29%  -3.66%\par  Romanian leu              