\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mostly stable, Crown dips on renewed  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  speculation\b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2013\par 17:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  little changed in quiet trade\par \par \uc2 * Slowing inflation revives chance of Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Investors await Polish court ruling on Wednesday\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/WARSAW, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The Czech crown dipped on Monday after data showing slower inflation revived the possibility that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could turn to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease policy further.\par \par \uc2 The zloty also weakened. Two of Poland's most dovish monetary policy setters said they saw limited scope for more interest rate cuts although analysts said the market was still pricing in two rate cuts over the next 12 months.\par \par \uc2 By 1518 GMT the zloty had inched 0.2 percent lower to 4.155 in light trade. The crown eased 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Market participants are also awaiting a court verdict expected in Poland this week that could affect monetary policy in the region's largest economy if it forces Jan Winiecki, who has blocked aggressive policy easing, to leave the bank's rate-setting council.\par \par \uc2 The court is scheduled to rule on whether Winiecki libelled a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor. Winiecki disputes the charges. If the court rules against him, the Senate, or upper house of parliament, will name a replacement.\par \par \uc2 The ruling could be delivered on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The government has been calling on the bank to cut rates further to support the economy and the ruling coalition has the majority in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 "The court ruling may negatively impact the zloty. The key question is who would replace Winiecki if he was dismissed," said a Warsaw-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, the forint eased 0.2 percent to 291.19 per euro, unmoved after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  ratings agency kept the country's rating in "junk" territory with a negative outlook due to weak growth prospects for the contracting economy.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warning on Hungary comes just as the most indebted central European country readies for a possible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond issue after Budapest's talks with the IMF about a financing backstop collapsed last year due to policy differences.\par \par \uc2 Central European economies are struggling to get or stay out of recession as the region suffers slowing trade with the crisis-hit euro zone and weaker consumer sentiment at home thanks to government belt-tightening.\par \par \uc2 Markets will look ahead to fourth-quarter gross domestic product readings in the Czech Republic, Hungary and Romania on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Data on Monday showed that the annual Czech inflation rate fell below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (CNB) 2 percent target for the first time in 15 months, which analysts said pointed to the need for easier monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Czech policymakers have made clear since cutting rates to "technical zero" in November that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown would be the next preferred way to ease policy to help the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2 "With the crown rebound after the board meeting last week, the monetary conditions are actually somewhat tighter at this moment," \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  analyst Stanislava Pravdova said.\par \par \uc2 "We think the CNB should step up its rhetoric again (or it risks) seriously undershooting its inflation target."\par \par \uc2 The crown has gained 2 percent since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled on Wednesday that further monetary easing was less urgent, quashing expectations it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu - which has gained 3 percent since December while other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region have dropped in that time because of falling interest rates - was down 0.1 percent at 4.397 to the euro on Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2013 \par Czech crown        25.233    25.221   -0.05%    -0.73%\par Polish zloty       4.155     4.145    -0.24%    -1.95%\par Hungarian forint   291.19    290.75   -0.15%    -0.08%\par Croatian kuna      7.576     7.575    -0.01%    -0.33%\par Romanian leu       4.397     4.393    -0.09%   +1.05%\par Serbian dinar      111.58    111.78   +0.18%   +0.65%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    0 basis points to  8bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    0 basis points to  +58bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +113bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds \par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR   +5 basis points to  +321bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR   +8 basis points to  +300bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR   +6 basis points to  +243bps over bmk*\par Hun