\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Crown hits high as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  risk fades\b0\par\par\uc2 864 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2013\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail on \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 * Crown firms as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears ease on cbank comment\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  yields rise, push leu to one-month low\par \par \uc2 * Forint recovers from weak data, investors await \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond\par \par \uc2 By Krisztina Than and Sam Cage\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST/BUCHAREST, Feb 7 (Reuters) - The Czech crown extended strong gains on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased fears it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while a rally in Romanian debt stalled and knocked the leu.\par \par \uc2 The crown extended gains from the previous session, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said recent weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  meant further monetary easing was less urgent, and rose a further 0.5 percent by 1429 GMT to 25.228 per euro, having hit a one-month high.\par \par \uc2 With rates at a "technical zero" since November, Czech policymakers have made clear that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown would be their next preferred way to ease policy in order to spur spending to boost the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2 "For a market which has been speculating for months now on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  (the bank's comments have) been a hit," \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2  fixed income trader Dalimil Vyskovsky said.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened massively in a short time and rates have jumped on both IRS and bonds. We think the move might soon prove to be exaggerated, though."\par \par \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  on Wednesday squashed expectations for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the bank had flagged earlier, saying further monetary easing may still be needed but looked less urgent.\par \par \uc2 Ceska Sporitelna\uc2  analyst Martin Lobotka recommended locking in profits on a recent short EUR/CZK recommendation.\par \par \uc2 "In the coming months, the bank will wait to see whether leading indicators translate into a better macro picture and will hold the crown between 25.20 and 25.70," he said in a note.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA RALLY STALLS\par \par \uc2 Thursday also saw a rally stall in Romanian debt which had sliced 100 basis points from yields after a convincing December election win for the leftist government eased political uncertainties. The leu was also lower.\par \par \uc2 Inclusion in a key \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  emerging market debt index had also supported Romanian bonds, but yields have now started to rise again as traders lock in profits.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry sold five-year paper on Thursday at 5.79 percent, a higher cost of funds than the 5.4 percent secured at the last auction on January 17.\par \par \uc2 ING said the recent weakening in bonds could be a buying opportunity and forecast yields on three- and five-year paper would fall back to 5.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The rally in bonds had pushed the leu to a one-year high in January but it has started to slip back and fell 0.4 percent to hit a one-month low of 4.415 per euro.\par \par \uc2 "The leu was the best performer so far this year among CEE peers so a correction had been expected," said a Bucharest dealer.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty and the forint tracked the crown higher, with the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounding from an initial fall to 294.94 after industrial output figures showed the biggest annual fall in more than three years.\par \par \uc2 The forint firmed 0.4 percent versus the euro to 292.9 and the government bond market also shrugged off the figures. Hungary sold more than planned at auctions on Thursday, with the market waiting on a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond issue in which Hungary may seek to raise as much as $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2013 \par Czech crown                  25.228    25.361  +0.53%    -0.71%\par Polish zloty                 4.169    4.181  +0.29%    -2.28%\par Hungarian forint             292.9    294.15  +0.43%    -0.66%\par Croatian kuna                7.575    7.584  +0.12%    -0.32%\par Romanian leu                 4.401    4.384   -0.39%   +0.95%\par Serbian dinar                111.42    111.16   -0.23%   +0.79%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +2 basis points to  9bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ6YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +55bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR    -3 basis points to  +39bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +520bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +4 basis points to  +534bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR +1 basis points to  +484bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters at 1