\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Joining Index Boosts  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2 , but  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Watch Begins\b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2013\par 21:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 15:42 EST - Viktor Szabo of \uc2 Aberdeen Asset Management\uc2  expects more flows to enter Romania's local bond market now that the country is set to join \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's emerging-market local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond index in a few months. In addition, Romania is expected to reach a deal with the IMF to replace its expiring backup financing agreement. Those factors will likely prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Szabo says there's potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  down the road. Given still-weak growth in \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- known for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past -- may not be so keen to see \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. Aberdeen started buying Romanian local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bonds in December, and purchased additional bonds on the secondary market last week. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) [ 18-01-13 2043GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130118e91i000s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
