\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-CZK near six-month low on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk\b0\par\par\uc2 995 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2013\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Czech crown falls as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  flags \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again\par \par \uc2 * Polish bonds fall on suggestion of pause in easing\par \par \uc2 * Leu firms to 9-month high on IMF deal hope\par \par \uc2 * Hungary raises bond sale, some think \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy\par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Sandor Peto and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST/WARSAW, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked the Czech crown, while Polish bond yields rose sharply on Thursday after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested it might halt cuts to borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  on Wednesday reiterated the bank's position that it is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if monetary policy needs to be eased further after interest rates were cut close to zero.\par \par \uc2 The crown fell to a six-month low against the euro, but regained some ground later. At 1436 GMT it was bid at 25.619, 0.5 percent weaker from Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A Prague dealer said the early weakening was fuelled by Singer's comments and a break through a technical level at 25.6-65 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 "There were foreign names heavily buying (euros) this morning between 25.650-750. On the other hand we see increased selling activity from local corporates," the dealer said. "It will probably at least slow down further crown weakening."\par \par \uc2 The crown is near levels where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to the 25.62 consensus estimate in a December Reuters poll, although a wide range of analyst estimates, from 24.5 to 27, showed high uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 Polish bonds continued to weaken for the second consecutive day as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled a pause in an easing cycle.\par \par \uc2 The Monetary Policy Council cut interest rates for the third time in a row on Wednesday, bringing the key rate to 4.0 percent but said it would probably soon pause its easing campaign.\par \par \uc2 Since then, bond yields have jumped by some 20 basis points at the shorter end of the curve and market players say it may just be the beginning of the trend.\par \par \uc2 "Risk that there will be a sharper sell-off on the bond market has grown markedly after yesterday's (comments) by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one Warsaw-based fixed income dealer.\par \par \uc2 Poland's 12x15 forward rate agreements are pricing in a total of 75 basis points more of interest rate cuts over a year and if the bank decides to end the cycle, many investors will decide to close their positions, market players say.\par \par \uc2 Hungary meanwhile increased the size of its first 2013 government bond sale by half as expectations that rates will fall and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might start buying bonds boosted investor demand.\par \par \uc2 Romania also sold more of its debt on Thursday thanks to greater political stability and prospects of a new \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  deal.\par \par \uc2 TIME FOR FALLS?\par \par \uc2 Hopes an international credit line will be secured have also boosted the leu which gained some 0.6 percent to the euro, hitting a nine-month high.\par \par \uc2 It has broken the level of 4.4 percent it had tested repeatedly since late December, when a clear election win gave the government a mandate to negotiate a new IMF deal.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Viktor Ponta makes a speech at 1600 GMT in which he may give details of the credit talks with the IMF and this year's budget, which has not yet been passed by parliament.\par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region were in the red on Thursday, with Hungary's forint down some 0.8 percent and the Polish zloty 0.3 percent weaker.\par \par \uc2 The two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were the region's top gainers last year, rising 9.5 percent and 7.7 percent respectively as investors sought healthy returns from high-yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 But easier monetary policy and - in some cases - countries' willingness to weaken their units has cooled the market's appetite for CEE assets and market players say scope for further strengthening is limited.\par \par \uc2 "I would tend to think that HUF, PLN and CZK would lead regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker - watch also for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BNR in \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stem recent appreciation and just take the heat out of hot money inflows," Timothy Ash, economist at Standard PLC wrote in a note. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2012 \par Czech crown       25.619   25.504   -0.45%    -2.23%\par Polish zloty       4.088    4.077   -0.27%    -0.34%\par Hungarian forint 291.97   