\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-Czech crown rebounds after mild cbank comments\b0\par\par\uc2 882 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2012\par 17:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  news conference, new prices)\par \par \uc2 * Czech cbank keeps rates on hold as expected\par \par \uc2 * Crown rebounds as cbank does not mention \b \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Leu slips as \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  delays IMF-agreed privatisation\par \par \uc2 * Positive global mood underpins other \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stocks\par \par \uc2 By Sam Cage and Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/BUDAPEST, Dec 19 (Reuters) - The crown regained ground on Wednesday to trade flat on the day after the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept interest rates on hold near zero but stayed mum about market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors watched closely whether the bank would step up its earlier rhetoric on possible crown selling. But Governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  did not signal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a news conference after the rate decision.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu meanwhile slipped from three-month highs after the new government delayed sales of state assets agreed with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , raising doubts about its commitment to a new IMF pact.\par \par \uc2 Progress in U.S. budget talks increased investors' risk appetite, supporting other emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equities.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its two-week repo rate\par \par \uc2 unchanged at 0.05 percent after slashing the benchmark rate earlier this year to support the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2 The bank's economic forecast has shifted from balanced to slightly anti-inflationary, but the change is small, he said.\par \par \uc2 "The forecast assumes looser monetary conditions, (moving to) the bottom, around the middle of the next year," Singer said, but he declined to forecast any monetary policy measures.\par \par \uc2 Erste Group\uc2  said in a note that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "did what it could and now it can pretty much sit and wait."\par \par \uc2 Dealers have said that investors would start to buy euros near crown levels at 25 against the euro. The crown was bid at 25.177 against the euro, off intra-day lows at 25.248.\par \par \uc2 "I think people want to see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cannot cope with the fact that it will not come soon," a Prague dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Other central banks in the region have also lowered borrowing costs to counter economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA'S IMF DEAL THREATENED\par \par \uc2 The leu eased 0.1 percent to the euro to 4.47.\par \par \uc2 "On the one hand, (the move in the leu reflects) commercial needs at the end of the year, and on the other the news that IMF-agreed privatisations have been postponed has taken a toll," said a Bucharest dealer.\par \par \uc2 Leftist Prime Minister Victor Ponta, whose government is set to be approved by parliament on Friday following a Dec. 9 election, had assured investors he would replace Romania's 5 billion euro IMF deal, which expires in early 2013.\par \par \uc2 But the government's announcement that it had postponed the sale of minority stakes in several state-controlled companies by a year, to end-2013, and a proposal to split the finance ministry, could complicate that process.\par \par \uc2 The IMF has regularly criticised the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's second-poorest member for failing to sell and reform its inefficient and oversized state sector, which holds back an economy that is only slowly emerging from a deep recession.\par \par \uc2 A positive global mood underpinned the Polish zloty\par \par \uc2 and the Hungarian forint amid expectations of more aggressive monetary stimulus from the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and signs of progress in resolving the U.S. budget logjam.\par \par \uc2 The zloty hovered around its highest since early October, rising 0.3 percent to 4.076, and the forint was up 0.4 percent, recouping some of this week's losses ahead of a meeting where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its base rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2012 \par Czech crown                 25.177   25.171   -0.02%   +1.46%\par Polish zloty                 4.076    4.088   +0.29%   +9.54%\par Hungarian forint           286.96   288.1     +0.4%    +9.63%\par Croatian kuna                7.531    7.535   +0.05%   -0.2%\par Romanian leu                 4.47     4.464   -0.13%   -3.34%\par Serbian dinar              113.23   113.01   -0.19%    -5.55%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +3 basis points to  24bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +50bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +111bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR    -3 basis points to  +563bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR    -9 basis points to  +561bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR  -9 basis 