\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Forint, zloty down on rate cut prospects\b0\par\par\uc2 845 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2012\par 12:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Hungary's c.bank seen cutting rates next week after low CPI\par \par \uc2 * Czech cbankers point to crown weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * All eyes on more stimulus in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects PM nomination after Sunday vote\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Dec 12 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint and Polish zloty fell against the euro on Wednesday driven by rate cut expectations, while the Czech crown shrugged off \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments pointing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at weakening the unit to support a fragile economy.\par \par \uc2 Prospects of Hungarian and Polish rate cuts outweighed expectations the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will announce a fresh round of bond buying with newly created money later on Wednesday, which were supporting riskier assets worldwide.\par \par \uc2 The forint and zloty are up 11 and 9 percent respectively year to date, having benefitted from a yield chase by investors outside western markets.\par \par \uc2 But traders said Tuesday data showing Hungarian inflation fell to 5.2 percent in November should bolster arguments for a fifth consecutive rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Next rate meeting takes place on Tuesday and given the lower inflation, the rather stable forint, despite recurrent cuts, as well as continued dovish comments from MPC members, we expect another cut by 25 basis points to 5.75 percent next week," SEB said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "We anticipate further cuts in the beginning of 2013 to front-load the easing cycle and expect the rate to bottom at 5.25 percent."\par \par \uc2 Poland too has cut its key rate twice this year to 4.25 percent, the lowest since May 2011.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday central banker Andrzej Kazmierczak, seen as one of the staunchest hawks among policymakers, said it was too early to speak about further cuts. But Governor Marek Belka said on Tuesday the bank was "very likely" to cut rates further to boost the slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 Market interest rates fully price in further cuts totalling 125 basis points over the next twelve months in Warsaw.\par \par \uc2 By 1045 GMT, the forint and zloty were each down 0.2 percent to the euro.\par \par \uc2 CZECH \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice-Governor Vladimir Tomsik said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown were the most efficient tool for further monetary easing, after the bank cut its main rate to a record low 0.05 percent last month.\par \par \uc2 Even the bank's most ardent hawk and monetary policy easing opponent weighed in on Wednesday saying she would support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on condition benefits to exporters would outweigh risks from higher prices.\par \par \uc2 Czech short-end yields dipped to fresh record lows, but the crown was up 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 "As long as there are voices from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary, then we should not be surprised if it really happens," \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2  analyst Jan Vejmelek said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "So far I have the feeling that market players are rather underestimating this risk."\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu was 0.2 percent stronger but still volatile as investors wait to see who President Traian Basescu will ask to form a government after Prime Minister Victor Ponta's coalition won two-thirds of seats in a parliamentary election.\par \par \uc2 The ruling leftist alliance has said it wants Ponta to be reappointed, but analysts said Basescu, locked in a power struggle with the prime minister, may try to split the parties by nominating someone else. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2012 \par Czech crown                  25.244    25.249  +0.02%   +1.19%\par Polish zloty                 4.096    4.085   -0.27%   +9%\par Hungarian forint             282.35    281.91   -0.16%   +11.42%\par Croatian kuna                7.53    7.522   -0.11%    -0.19%\par Romanian leu                 4.529    4.541  +0.26%    -4.59%\par Serbian dinar                113.93    113.73   -0.18%    -6.13%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    -11 basis points to  22bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ6YT=RR    -4 basis points to  +57bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR    -1 basis points to  +66bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +569bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR    -2 basis points to  +577bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR +4 basis points to  +501bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent. All data taken from Reuters at 1211 CET. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic close at 1700 GMT. For related news and prices, click on the \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par codes in brackets: All emerging market news   \par Spot \f28 \b \highlig