\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Rally on Polish bonds continues, CZK recoups losses\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2012\par 16:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Polish 5-yr bond yields at record low\par \par \uc2 * Czech c.bank governor says bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells planned 250 mln lei in 3-yr bonds\par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/WARSAW, Oct 11 (Reuters) - Polish 5-year bonds hit record lows on Thursday on expectations the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon cut borrowing costs, while the Czech crown recouped early losses tracking a stronger euro.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the crown fell after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  said the bank may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there was a risk of long-term deflation pressure.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region were mostly firmer in afternoon trade though traders said worries over Spain persist.\par \par \uc2 Expectations of lower interest rates in Hungary and Poland are pointing to weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in those regions and bond yields are near record lows in Poland and the Czech Republic.\par \par \uc2 "Rally on Polish bonds continues and every single effort of setting against the trend ends up badly," said Bartlomiej Wit, chief fixed income dealer at \uc2 ING Bank Slaski\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By 1316 GMT the crown, the Polish zloty and Hungary's forint each added some 0.2 percent to the euro while Romania's leu edged some 0.2 percent lower.\par \par \uc2 Minutes from the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Sept. 27 meeting, released last week, showed that the governing board was still divided over whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown and employ more monetary easing to prop up the recession-hit economy.\par \par \uc2 Years of austerity are taking a toll on the Czech economy and other economies in the region are fighting to get out of or avoid recession. The export-driven region is also struggling with slowing trade with the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 In Poland, a speech by Prime Minister Donald Tusk on Friday was keenly awaited, as he is expected to announce some measures to try to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, the forint was steady, shrugging off data showing the headline inflation rate jumped to 6.6 percent, the highest in over four years. Hungary has cut its interest rates, the highest in the European Union, for two months in a row.\par \par \uc2 Hungary sold nearly 1.5 times as much 12-month paper as originally planned and average yields fell 23 basis points from the previous auction two weeks ago. Yields on the secondary market also fell, and the government plans to launch a new three-year euro-denominated bond.\par \par \uc2 Budapest, which is still wrangling with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  over a financing deal analysts say is needed to bring its borrowing costs back down to manageable levels, has not tapped international markets so far this year.\par \par \uc2 "Regardless of the high inflation data, which surpassed already high market projections, expectations for interest rate cuts have not diminished," said a Budapest fixed income trader.\par \par \uc2 "If Hungary wants, it can come out with a euro bond, and if storm clouds are gathering, there is still the IMF as an alternative."\par \par \uc2 Romania sold a planned 250 million lei in three-year treasury bonds, with the average accepted yield some 26 basis points lower compared to the level accepted at the last tender of the paper in February. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2012 \par Czech crown       24.855   24.908  +0.21%   +2.78%\par Polish zloty       4.088    4.095  +0.17%   +9.21%\par Hungarian forint 281.75   282.35   +0.21%   +11.66%\par Croatian kuna      7.52     7.469  -0.68%   -0.06%\par Romanian leu       4.567    4.56   -0.15%   -5.39%\par Serbian dinar    113.5    113.6    +0.09%   -5.77%\par \par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    0 basis points to  45bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ6YT=RR   +4 basis points to  +76bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR   +5 basis points to  +86bps over bmk*\par \par Polish treasury bonds \par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +394bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR    -2 basis points to  +359bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR    -5 basis points to  +305bps over bmk*\par \par Hungarian treasury bonds \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR    -7 basis points to  +631bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR    -4 basis points to  +602bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR  -4 basis points to  +555bps over bmk*\par *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\par All data taken from Reuters at 1516 CET.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic \par close at 1600 GMT.   \par For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets: All\par emerging market news   \par Spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates\par Eastern Europe spot \f28 