\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romania president accuses government of power grab\b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2012\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Government trying to suspend, impeach president\par \par \uc2 * President says govt seeks control of judiciary\par \par \uc2 * Political row pressures \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , debt costs\par \par \uc2 * Thousands rally in central Bucharest\par \par \uc2 (Adds rallies, quotes, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Sam Cage and Luiza Ilie\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, July 5 (Reuters) - Romania's president accused the government on Thursday of using an attempt to impeach him as a way of grabbing control of the judiciary and other state institutions.\par \par \uc2 The leftist Social-Liberal Union (USL) government is set to use its parliamentary majority to vote on Friday to suspend right-winger Traian Basescu. A referendum would then be held on his impeachment within a month.\par \par \uc2 The impeachment threat is part of a wider political clash that has paralysed lawmaking and raised doubts over Romania's ability to keep to a 5 billion euro International Monetary Fund-led aid deal - hurting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and increasing debt costs.\par \par \uc2 Basescu told parliament: "The major objective of this suspension is to put the justice system and state institutions under the control of parties in the USL."\par \par \uc2 Some 2,000 supporters of the opposition Democrat-Liberals (PDL) backing Basescu gathered in downtown Bucharest, shouting anti-government slogans. In another square, people backing Prime Minister Victor Ponta shouted: "Out with Basescu."\par \par \uc2 In power since May, after the previous, centre-right government collapsed, the USL, led by Ponta, Romania's third prime minister in four months, is favourite to win an election late this year.\par \par \uc2 Opponents accuse him of trying to cling to power, but many people are tired of an austerity drive enforced by a centre-right government in 2010.\par \par \uc2 "We are witnessing a systematic attack on state institutions \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ... now they attack presidency and the final target is to\par subordinate justice," newly elected PDL leader Vasile   Blaga\par told the gathering.     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The USL passed a law to make it easier to impeach Basescu, whose position is ceremonial but who influenced the previous government's austerity policies. In the impeachment request, USL lawmakers said the president broke the constitution and pressured judges.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The new law, still pending judgment in the constitutional court, would make it possible for a simple majority of voters to impeach a president in a referendum, rather than requiring a majority of the entire electorate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In late afternoon, the government approved a decree setting a simple voting majority for referendums. It is not clear whether the decree or the court verdict, likely due on Monday, will prevail.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both reverse previous legislation by the PDL, which has close links to the president and is now in opposition. The PDL had switched the referendum rule to a majority of the electorate after a previous attempt to unseat Basescu in 2007.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basescu would probably lose the referendum and his post if the new legislation is enforced, but easily survive if the old threshold is kept.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POWER GRAB\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ponta did not attend the parliamentary debate on Thursday, seeking instead to reassure investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I am not in parliament for a political debate but I am here with you because I feel that in this type of political battle it is essential to maintain economic balance," Ponta told a meeting of investors, according to news agency Agerpres.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The USL has come under severe pressure itself. Ponta faces calls to resign over plagiarism charges and the government had to back down from an attempt to replace judges on the constitutional court, after international criticism.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The president of the Venice Commission, the Council of Europe's advisory body on constitutional matters, issued a statement expressing "deep concern (at) various attempts to exercise pressure on the Constitutional Court of Romania and to undermine its independence".\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The leu struck a new record low on Thursday beyond 4.492 per euro, while yields rose at a two-year Romanian bond sale, reflecting rising investor concern.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Romania\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  looks now rather like Ukraine or Belarus than a CEE state. It looks everyone wants to get out and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems to be present on the offer side as it wants to prevent sharp swings," a dealer at a foreign bank in Bucharest said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Radu Marinas; Editing by Alison Williams)\f28 \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA-POLITICS/ (PIX, TV) (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | G | M | RDN | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | RNA | RNP | DNP | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120705e875000ne\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
