\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Romanian Leu Will Continue To Underperform -BBH\b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2012\par 22:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 4:36 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a first line of defense to bring the leu back to its comfort zone of RON4.40/euro, says Win Thin of BBH, as it did Wednesday. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in somewhat unchartered territory and the economic backdrop is unsupportive. Exports make up more than 1/3 of Romania's GDP, and trade with the euro zone is a sizeable part of that. While the country has been easing rates to support growth, it can't do much more without hurting the economy. "Romania is simply facing the same challenges as the euro zone is, and that is a continued emphasis on austerity even as growth slows and social unrest rises," says Thin. "This makes for a potentially destabilizing mix of economic and political turmoil." (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com [ 02-05-12 2036GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120502e852001c8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
