\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Romania c.bank to cut rates for 4th month\b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 14:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Bank meets Thursday, March 29, no specific time set\par \par \uc2  * Expected to cut rates by 25 bps to 5.25 pct\par \par \uc2  * For full poll see or  \par \par \uc2  By Ioana Patran\par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, March 23 (Reuters) - Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely cut interest rates for the fourth month running next week and once more before the middle of the year, but caution over the impact of global fuel prices and a parliamentary election may make it pause thereafter.\par \par \uc2  Official borrowing costs in the European Union's second poorest member state are already at an all-time low of 5.5 percent as the bank seeks to reboot an economy still only recovering slowly from a collapse in 2009 that forced it to seek IMF support. \par \par \uc2  All but one of 16 analysts polled by Reuters said the bank would cut rates by another quarter-point at its March meeting and 12 said it would cut again before the end of the second quarter.\par \par \uc2  Those moves are justified by an expected fall in inflation to another record low this month, after reaching 2.6 percent in February, leaving "real" interest rates still relatively high.\par \par \uc2  "The economy needs stimulus for growth and of course lower interest rates help financing the public deficit, reducing the cost of public debt," said Georgiana Constantinescu, analyst at Credit Europe Bank in Bucharest.\par \par \uc2  A cold snap earlier this year when temperatures plunged below minus 20 degrees Celsius and snow storms blocked roads, railways and ports has hurt output and could push the economy into negative territory in the first quarter.\par \par \uc2  Romanian exporters are facing falling demand from the euro zone, its main trade partner, and the economy is facing a second consecutive quarterly contraction that would put it briefly back into recession. \par \par \uc2  The government expects growth of 1.5-2 percent for the whole of 2012, down from a 2.5 percent expansion last year. \par \par \uc2  All but four of the sixteen analysts polled by Reuters expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to deliver another quarter point cut after the March 29 meeting, bringing borrowing costs to 5 percent by the end of the second quarter \par \par \uc2  However, some said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stop its easing cycle after its March meeting, as inflationary risks stemming from fuel prices, a weak leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an upcoming parliamentary election were tilted to the upside.\par \par \uc2  "We are mulling a revision of our reference rate forecast as global oil prices are amplified by a weak leu and electoral pressures loom throughout the next eight months," said Mihai Patrulescu, economist at \uc2 Bancpost\uc2  in Bucharest.\par \par \uc2  "At the next week's meeting we could see the last cut this year."\par \par \uc2  Romania's leu hit a 21-month low last week against the euro and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly to curb its move.\par \par \uc2  The leu, emerging Europe's most stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011, has failed to benefit from a sharp rebound in riskier assets so far this year as investor interest was limited mainly by the threat of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem volatility. \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RATES/ (PREVIEW) | ABN | D | M | RDN | E | RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120323e83n000q8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
