\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Leu flirts with 21-month low, Fitch warns Hungary\b0\par\par\uc2 1,019 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Leu close to 21-month low after rate cuts\par \par \uc2 * Dealers say Romanian cbank supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Fitch says could cut Hungary if no IMF deal\par \par \uc2 (Updates with Fitch report, new prices)\par \par \uc2 By Sam Cage and Michael Winfrey\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/PRAGUE, March 16 (Reuters) - Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  inched lower on Friday, with Romania's leu hovering near a 21-month low and the forint under the microscope after rating agency Fitch said Hungary could face another credit downgrade.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors were on alert for further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Serbia, where the dinar\par \par \uc2 has fallen due to uncertainty over the outcome of parliamentary elections scheduled for May.\par \par \uc2 The leu was the emerging European Union's most stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the euro zone debt crisis raged in 2011, but it has failed to benefit from a sharp rebound in riskier assets this year on a brightening global economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 Poland's zloty and the Hungarian forint have led the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains this year, each rising more than 8 percent, with the Czech crown following.\par \par \uc2 The leu, however is down 1.25 percent in that time. It was virtually flat on the session at 4.38 per euro at 1351 GMT, less than 1 percent off an all-time low of 4.4023 hit during Romania's own funding crisis in 2010, when the government austerity measures forced the economy into a deep recession.\par \par \uc2 "It looks exciting, finally, for the EURRON. Volumes yesterday and today were at least four times larger than the average of the previous 2-3 weeks," said a Bucharest dealer.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut interest rates to a record low 5.5 percent and bond yields have fallen across the curve, to 6.29 percent on five-year paper. The bank also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via third parties to prop up the leu at 4.39 per euro on Thursday and was also active on Friday, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Behind this weakening move could be slightly looser control of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it could be a signal that the RON is likely to trade in a wider range - probably one between 4.32-4.42/EUR," said ING analyst Vlad Muscalu.\par \par \uc2 FITCH ON HUNGARY\par \par \uc2 Hungarian markets, the most volatile in the region in 2012 as the government struggles to secure a new credit line from the European Union and IMF, were closed and the forint was down around 0.1 percent on the day in offshore trade.\par \par \uc2 The country has come under fire due to a string of policy decisions from Prime Minister Viktor Orban's government that critics say have flouted budget rules and could undermine democracy.\par \par \uc2 EU finance ministers moved to freeze almost half a billion euros in development funds this week unless Budapest could present it with a credible fiscal plan by June.\par \par \uc2 That drew an angry retort from Orban, who told tens of thousands of supporters at rally on Thursday they would not be treated as second-class European citizens.\par \par \uc2 Fitch said it expected Orban to bow to EU pressure to set out a credible fiscal reduction plan this spring so it could start aid talks and unfreeze the development funds.\par \par \uc2 But even if it does, doubts will remain about whether Budapest can submit to the IMF's strict conditionality, Fitch said, adding failure to secure the loan could prompt a downgrade to Hungary's credit rating, which is already in 'junk' territory.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown was down 0.1 percent at 24.522 per euro, and the Polish zloty was 0.3 percent weaker at 4.135.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also supported its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year as the problems in the euro zone - emerging Europe's main trade and banking partner - hurt the zloty, and Governor Marek Belka said he believed it had reduced volatility by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The biggest concern is the euro zone," Belka said during an economic forum in Prague, adding that Poland's relatively high level of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans continued to be a cause for worry.\par \par \uc2 Dealers say Serbia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dinar this week. The outcome of May's election could have a major impact on the Balkan country's EU candidacy and talks over a backstop loan from the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT---------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2012 \par Czech crown                  24.522  24.503   -0.08%   +4.17%\par Polish zloty                 4.135    4.123   -0.29%   +7.97%\par Hungarian forint             290.6   290.38   -0.08%   +8.26%\par Croatian kuna                7.526    7.512   -0.19%   -0.14%\par Romanian leu                 4.