\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Forint leads gains in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , Romanian leu falls\b0\par\par\uc2 1,088 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 18:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds Romania)\par \par \uc2 * Romanian leu down 0.3 pct vs. euro, hits 20-mth low\par \par \uc2 * Polish yields rise for 2nd day, zloty off lows\par \par \uc2 * Crown firm, forint up as local markets closed\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/WARSAW, March 15 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint led gains in central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday as they rebounded thanks to a stronger euro, getting a break from a bout of profit taking this week that has halted a rally since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 The Romanian leu bucked the trend, however, falling to a 20-month low versus the euro as a looming economic slowdown and interest rate cuts are making the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive.\par \par \uc2 Central European stocks were mixed, while Polish bond yields rose 4 basis points, up for a second day after higher-than-expected inflation data this week dampened expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut interest rates later this year.\par \par \uc2 By 1459 GMT, the forint had gained 0.6 percent to 290.83 to the euro, while the Polish zloty, the region's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was up 0.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 "In the mid-term the zloty may appreciate somewhat, but I would not expect strong gains as we are in the phase of slowing economic activity and elections in Greece are around the corner," said Dorota Strauch, an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Raiffeisen Bank Polska. Greek election could revive worries about Greek debt and tame global risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, local markets were closed for a national holiday with rallies expected to be held both for and against Prime Minister Viktor Orban's government, which is struggling to get a credit line from the European Union and \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  to ease borrowing strains.\par \par \uc2 Unease over Budapest's attempts to counter EU and IMF criticism of its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation - which is holding up aid talks - has prompted many investors to be more cautious on eastern Europe, where exports are being hit by the debt crisis in its key export market, the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Czech crown added 0.5 percent to 24.521 to the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The crown is playing catch-up with the forint and the zloty's more than 8 percent gains this year, but dealers say it would be difficult to break firmer than its five-month high of 24.500.\par \par \uc2 "There is still nice (euro) support around 24.500/550, and I see quite good demand to buy (euro) below 24.600," \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2  dealer Lubos Kolarik said.\par \par \uc2 "There are also nice offers above 24.630/640, so there has been some nice volume in this range that is two-way at the moment. People rather tend to buy dips than sell rallies."\par \par \uc2 Czech bond yields rose on the long end. Rates are also up, tracking euro markets but also getting a lift from comments from central banker Kamil Janacek on Wednesday saying the record-low base rate could rise this year.\par \par \uc2 LEU FALLS\par \par \uc2 The Romanian leu fell 0.3 percent to the euro, hitting a multi-month low of 4.388 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 "I think we are seeing a combination of deleveraging flow with people closing out short EUR/RON bets," said Peter Attard Montalto, an economist at \uc2 Nomura International\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "People saw a divergence between Romania CDS and EURRON and thought RON should rally but it didn't, so now closing out and hitting stops," he also said, adding he expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week.\par \par \uc2 The leu has been the most stable emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past two years - as the euro zone debt crisis has made \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region volatile - partly due to the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 1.03 billion lei ($307 million) in five-year treasury bonds on Thursday, double the planned amount. The average yields fell 46 basis points from last month's tender, following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 The bank cut interest rates to a record low of 5.5 percent in February, further beefing up its support for a fragile economy that may suffer its second consecutive quarterly contraction in the first quarter of 2012.\par \par \uc2 In Serbia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the third consecutive day on Thursday to halt a weakening of the dinar against the euro, dealers and traders said.\par \par \uc2 Investor concerns are rising over who will win elections in Serbia in May. Whoever takes power could have a profound impact on policies ranging from Serbia's candidacy for the European Union to its negotiations over a 1 billion euro ($1.3 billion) backstop loan from the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 . ID:nL5E8EF1W3]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f