\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  down ahead of key euro summit\b0\par\par\uc2 1,032 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2011\par 17:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds fresh bond prices)\par \par \uc2 * Eyes on EU summit as debt crisis weighs on CEE\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  soften after recent selling pressure\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Radu Marinas\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, Oct 26 (Reuters) - European emerging\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged down against the euro on Wednesday and the forint fell to its lowest level since April 2009 with investors cautious\par \par \uc2 ahead of a crucial EU summit tasked with endorsing a plan to tackle the euro zone's debt crisis .\par \par \uc2 The incoming head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threw the euro zone a lifeline hours before the summit on Wednesday by signalling the bank would go on buying troubled states' bonds to combat market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Mario Draghi delivered the message that financial markets have been waiting for about the ECB's intentions as leaders of the 17-nation single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  area struggled to produce a comprehensive plan to resolve the bloc's sovereign debt woes.\par \par \uc2 [ID: nLDE79O03J ]\par \par \uc2 " In the next days and weeks we will watch whether European leaders have some concrete message to markets ," a Budapest-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 The forint fell 1.2 percent from its opening level to 302 against the euro by 1433 GMT , pressured by falls in the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fears over a potential ratings downgrade.\par \par \uc2 By 1448 GMT, the forint eased further, to 302.60 per euro according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 "The latest news about the euro zone bailout package were not good," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Budapest said.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian bonds eased after comment s from Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy about the risk of a downgrade of sovereign debt rating by one agency . [ID:nL5E7LQ394 ]\par \par \uc2 P olicymakers in central Europe foresee slowing economies and lower state revenues next year due partly to the euro zone's debt troubles. This has put a drag on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that, apart from of the Czech crown, have lost ground in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy said on Wednesday the economy needs a boost if it is to reach a goal of 1.5 percent growth in 2012.\par \par \uc2 His comments echoed the tone of Czech Finance Minister Miroslav Kalousek, who said on Tuesday the government may have to come up with more savings measures next year to keep to its budget deficit goals.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown fell 0.6 percent to 24. 05 per\par \par \uc2 euro.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , caught in a policy bind of rising risk premiums and a weak forint, held its key rate at 6 percent on Tuesday. Markets see chances of a hike ahead even with the slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 "I'm not convinced they can do without a rate hike for much longer, be it an emergency hike or a slow trickle of hikes," a Budapest dealer said.\par \par \uc2 PROSPECTS DIM\par \par \uc2 The forint has led a retreat in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Sept. 1, falling more than 8 percent as Europe's policymakers struggle to reach agreement on the best way to contain a sovereign debt crisis that began two years ago in Greece.\par \par \uc2 "It is clear that the market is no longer expecting the comprehensive solution that was preannounced a few weeks ago," KBC said.\par \par \uc2 "So, it is not excluded that the wait-and-see mode might continue as there won't be enough 'hard stuff' to react to."\par \par \uc2 Poland's zloty traded 0.5 percent down at 4.36 on the day. Romania's leu\par \par \uc2 edged down 0. 4 percent.\par \par \uc2 A Bucharest dealer said risk of leu \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in place after central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Poland stepped in over the past month to rescue \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from lows.\par \par \uc2 "The market is calm due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  the other days and if there is no client to take the lead," a Bucharest dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Romanian budget data on Tuesday showed the state can easily meet its IMF-agreed target of a deficit of 4.4 percent this year, but prospects for next year are less certain.\par \par \uc2 "This should not be a major worry, yet, although a weaker growth outlook increases the risk for fiscal slippage next year," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Central European stock markets were mixed, hovering\par \par \uc2 around Tuesday's levels , while the Czech bourse\par \par \uc2 was up 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2011 \par Czech crown        25.066   24.906   -0.64%   -0.26%\par Polish zloty       4.393    4.368    -0.57%   -9.9%\par Hungarian forint   302.5    297.6    -1.62%   -8.11%\par Croatian kuna      7.483    7.485    +0.03%   -1.38%\par Romanian leu       4.338    4.32     -0.41%   -2.42%\par Serbian dinar     