\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romania - Factors to watch on Oct 20\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2011\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds press digest)\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Oct 20 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 DEBT AUCTION\par \par \uc2 Romania tenders 600 million lei ($190.9 million)in 3-year treasury bonds.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA, CHINA GUANGDONG DISCUSS NEW NUCLEAR UNITS\par \par \uc2 China Guangdong Nuclear Power Group\uc2  may invest in a project to add two more reactors at Romania's sole nuclear power plant in Cernavoda on the Danube river, Romania's economy ministry said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA GOVT APPROVES LUKOIL BLACK SEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 Romania's centrist coalition government approved on Wednesday a concession agreement for the oil exploration and development of two offshore blocks in the Black Sea with Russia's second-largest oil company LUKOIL .\par \par \uc2 IMF\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund released Romania's latest letter of intent under its 5.4 billion euro precautionary aid deal, which details plans for cutting the budget deficit and privatisations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.imf.org/External/NP/LOI/2011/ROU/091411.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.imf.org/External/NP/LOI/2011/ROU/091411.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 CEE MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  PULLS AWAY FROM \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  LEVELS\par \par \uc2 Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks rose on Wednesday on hopes that Europe will come up with new steps to tackle the euro zone debt crisis, pulling the leu and zloty away from levels that could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 POPULATION CENSUS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's population census will start on Thursday and the first results of the survey will be available next year.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 1\par \par \uc2 WIND ENERGY PARK\par \par \uc2 French company Filasa plans to build eleven wind energy park in the Romanian county of Suceava, with a total capacity of 516 MW and an investment of 780 million euros ($1.1 billion), a local official said.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 16\par \par \uc2 NOTE- For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see .\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\tab \par Romania Market Debt     Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       \tab \par Romania Market Report     Romanian money      \tab \par Emerging Market Debt  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \tab \par All Emerging Markets news CEE indicators  \tab \par All East Europe News        E.Europe equities     \tab \par TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   \tab \par TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  \tab \par Romanian indicators        \tab \par Main page of Reuters poll  \tab \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1 = 3.143 Romanian Lei) ($1 = 0.725 Euros)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111020e7ak000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
