\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romania - Factors to watch on Sept 28\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2011\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  GOVERNMENT MEETING\par \par \uc2  The centrist coalition government holds weekly meeting from 1200 GMT with no agenda available yet.\par \par \uc2  BRITAIN'S BUSINESS SECRETARY IN ROMANIA\par \par \uc2  Britain's Business Secretary Vince Cable starts a two day visit to Romania.\par \par \uc2  ROMANIA'S HIDROELECTRICA TO CUT ENERGY DELIVERIES\par \par \uc2  Romanian state-owned hydro power producer Hidroelectrica has declared force majeure due to drought and will cut deliveries to clients for the rest of the year, its general director was quoted on Tuesday as saying.\par \par \uc2  ROMANIA 2011 MAIZE CROP SEEN AT ABOUT 11 MLN T-AGMIN\par \par \uc2  Romania expects to reap 10.9 million tonnes of maize this year, up 21 percent on the year, and has so far harvested 3.6 million tonnes from 31 percent of the total area, the agriculture ministry said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  CEE MARKETS-SLIGHT RETURN OF RISK APPETITE LIFTS CEE ASSETS\par \par \uc2  The zloty and forint led emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher on Tuesday, benefiting from the return of some appetite for riskier assets and underpinned by the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region.\par \par \uc2  TRANSELECTRICA\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy ministry extended to Oct. 6 a deadline to receive bids from firms interested to advise on the secondary listing of a 15 percent stake in state-owned power grid operator \uc2 Transelectrica\uc2  .\par \par \uc2  The selected adviser could be announced in the first half of October, Victor Cazana, the head of the industry privatisation office said.\par \par \uc2  Ziarul Financiar, Page 5\par \par \uc2  CAR SALES\par \par \uc2  Domestic car sales were up 10.6 percent on the year in August to 7,800 units, data from the manufacturers' association showed. Sales were down 12 percent on the year to 60,000 cars in the first eight months of 2011.\par \par \uc2  Ziarul Financiar, Page 12\par \par \uc2  UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2  The unemployment rate is rising slightly from the previous 4.8 percent in August as seasonal jobs close but the figure will not exceed 5 percent this year, the head of Romania's employment agency said. Jurnalul National, Page 8\par \par \uc2  NOTE- For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see .\par \par \uc2  For other related news, double click on:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\tab \par Romania Market Debt     Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       \tab \par Romania Market Report     Romanian money      \tab \par Emerging Market Debt  Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \tab \par All Emerging Markets news CEE indicators  \tab \par All East Europe News        E.Europe equities     \tab \par TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   \tab \par TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  \tab \par Romanian indicators        \tab \par Main page of Reuters poll  \tab \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110928e79s0006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
