\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romania - Factors to watch on Sept 23\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 08:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 MONEY SUPPLY\par \par \uc2 Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to release money supply data for August.\par \par \uc2 EU STATES TO KEEP BORDERS WITH ROMANIA, BULGARIA\par \par \uc2 Romania and Bulgaria failed to persuade other European Union governments on Thursday to let them join Europe's passport-free travel zone, with opponents citing concerns about corruption and organised crime in the two Balkan states.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA SELLS 98.4 MLN LEI IN 10-YR T-BONDS\par \par \uc2 Romania sold a less than planned 98.4 million lei ($31.4 million) in 10-year treasury bonds on Thursday, with the average accepted yield at 7.65 percent, up from 7.59 percent at a previous tender on Aug. 25, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 CEE MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell broadly against the euro on Thursday, worrying regional central bankers who are struggling to manage the fallout in their financial markets from a slowdown in the world economy.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO STOP LEU SLIDE-DEALERS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped in indirectly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling euros via local banks on Thursday to temper the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall against the euro, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA ECONMIN SEES 2012 GROWTH AT 2.5-3 PCT\par \par \uc2 Romania's economy will probably grow by 2.5-3 percent in 2012, lower than initially estimated, Economy Minister Ion Ariton said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA TO HIKE GAS PRICES 8 PCT FOR INDUSTRY-REPORT\par \par \uc2 Romania will raise gas tariffs for industrial consumers by roughly 8 percent from October, its energy price regulator was quoted as saying on Thursday, as part of an IMF-agreed plan to eliminate price caps.\par \par \uc2 EU INDUSTRY COMMISSIONER IN ROMANIA\par \par \uc2 EU Industry Commissioner Antonio Tajani ends a two-day visit to Romania. He is expected to meet Prime Minister Emil Boc at 0730 GMT.\par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT PRESIDENT IN ROMANIA\par \par \uc2 European Parliament President Jerzy Buzek is in Bucharest and will meet Romanian officials on Friday.\par \par \uc2 OMV TO DIVEST 1 BLN EUR, SEES PRODUCTION GROWTH\par \par \uc2 Energy group OMV plans to divest 1 billion euros ($1,4 billion) of refining and marketing assets by 2014 as it shifts its portfolio towards exploration and production (E&P), it said at its capital markets day in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 *Chief Executive Gerhard Roiss said its Romanian Petrobrazi was the only refinery in which OMV was still investing.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 16\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN POST\par \par \uc2 The Belgian post could buy shares in Romania's postal office, sources said after Belgian Prime Minister Yves Leterme met Prime Minister Emil Boc on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Jurnalul National, Page 9\par \par \uc2 NOTE- For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see .\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\tab \par Romania Market Debt     Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       \tab \par Romania Market Report     Roma