\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Stronger Romania leu backed by fundamentals-cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 12:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank adviser says recent rise supported by economy\par \par \uc2 * Leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 10-month high versus euro\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say comments suggest leu may rise more\par \par \uc2 (Releads, adds more analyst comment, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Radu Marinas\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, March 22 (Reuters) - Romania's leu hit a 10-month high against the euro on Tuesday after an adviser to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu said recent gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflect increasing economic strength.\par \par \uc2 "The leu is very much in line with fundamentals," Lucian Croitoru told Reuters by telephone, in a rare comment by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The leu hit 4.1325 against the euro after his comment, its highest since May 4, 2010, and 0.6 percent higher on the day <EURRON=>.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said it could gain further, helping tame inflation fuelled by surging food and energy prices on global markets.\par \par \uc2 Regional peers' strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had allowed them to keep interest rates low as their economies recover strongly from the 2008 crisis, although Poland and Hungary have already raised rates and the Czech Republic is expected to follow.\par \par \uc2 Analysts and dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February to support the leu on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, raising doubts about whether 2011's 2.5 percent gain against the euro was supported by signs of economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Romania suffered a deep recession but the economy has shown signs of life this year, while the government has completed a 20 billion euro International Monetary Fund-led bailout and agreed a new precautionary deal.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been expected to cut interest rates to stimulate growth after holding them at a record low of 6.25 percent since May 2010 but some analysts have recently revised that view as a result of imported inflation.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said Croitoru's comments suggested there was room for further leu appreciation, particularly with the government looking more secure after surviving a fifth no-confidence vote last week and pushing through IMF-backed reforms.\par \par \uc2 ING said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could firm towards 4.05 per euro. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 ANALYSIS on Romania rate policy [ID:nLDE71O05N]\par \par \uc2 Romania govt survives censure vote [ID:nLDE72F1IU] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 "This proves what I've already been saying, that we would witness more appreciation of the leu against the euro," said ING analyst Nicolaie Alexandru-Chidesciuc.\par \par \uc2 The leu hit a five-month high against the euro, the main reference for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in late February after what dealers said was covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to counter rising prices.\par \par \uc2 "The (leu) firming has been initially engineered mostly by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Consequently, the leu has benefited from positive reports about \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Alexandru-Chidesciuc.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its end-2011 inflation forecast to 3.6 percent from a previous 3.4 percent last month, but held fire on more support for the country's struggling economy after a jump in prices caused by a rise in value-added tax last year.\par \par \uc2 "I do believe that in the new context of higher inflation with quite powerful pressures manifested, exchange rate appreciation could temper inflationary expectations," said Ionut Dumitru of Raiffeisen Bank in Bucharest.\par \par \uc2 Dumitru now sees the leu reaching 4.15 per euro at the end of June, after revising an early March prediction. <RO/POLL1>\par \par \uc2 "Romania looks better, fundamentals have been improving," Dumitru said. "Probably the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now has a higher degree of comfort to rein in inflation."\par \par \uc2 The IMF board will meet on March 25 to debate Romania's request to rubber stamp the new 5 billion euro aid agreement.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA-LEU/ (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110322e73m000ny\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
