\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Crown hits 22-mth high;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  helps leu\b0\par\par\uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 17:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Crown breaks resistance past 2010 highs\par \par \uc2 * Dealers say Romania cbank behind leu outperformance\par \par \uc2 * Hungary Econ Ministry reiterates budget pledge, bonds rise\par \par \uc2 (Recasts with crown, updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Marius Zaharia and Jason Hovet\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/PRAGUE, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Czech crown broke resistance levels to a 22-month high on Tuesday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  leu outperformed thanks to likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  even as weak stock markets dragged on other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A poor reading of Germany's ZEW economic sentiment indicator dragged on the region with investors worried the fragile export-driven recovery in emerging Europe may hit the wall, especially if fiscal cuts begin to hamper growth. Hungarian assets were boosted by comment from the Hungarian Economy Ministry cleared some confusion over Hungary's pledge to reduce its budget deficit next year, and whether it hinged on EU accounting changes.\par \par \uc2 The ministry said on Tuesday the country is committed to cutting its 2011 budget deficit to below 3 percent of gross domestic product regardless of a decision in Brussels on a proposed change in pension accounting rules. [ID:nBUD005497]\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy was also cited as saying the deficit reduction could be achieved without austerity.\par \par \uc2 Hungary government bond prices reversed an early decline and yields dropped back near three-week lows.\par \par \uc2 But the leu led gains in the region, rising 0.7 percent to a September high around 4.23 to the euro. Five dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was behind the move, with two estimating a tiny 100-150 million euros may have been sold. [ID:nLDE68D0W7]\par \par \uc2 "It moved more than 150 pips, with banks that are the usual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  instruments selling (euros) at a timing very similar to past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before the fixing," a dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The reasons for any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unclear, as the leu traded within the 4.2-4.3 per euro range seen as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's "comfort zone". Another dealer suspected the bank may fear second-round effects on inflation from a July VAT hike.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is suspected of constantly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market against both sharp weakening or firming since late 2008, was not available for comment.\par \par \uc2 CROWN PATH CLEAR\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The crown -- central Europe's top performer with a 7 percent\par gain this year and beating a 4 percent rise for the zloty --\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 broke 2010 highs around 24.630/620 per euro, which had provided resistance for the past month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the crown has benefitted from increased foreign demand for Czech bonds and treasury bills, which have dropped to historic lows since June on government austerity pledges. This has helped make the crown a safe haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in central Europe when risk appetite is low.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The crown added 0.5 percent to 24.516 per euro by 1449 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are starting to move in one direction," a Prague \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer said. "(The crown) is also getting good flow from the (debt) papers market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint rose 0.6 percent and extended a fifth straight session with gains after pledges to cut the deficit last week. This has helped bonds but dealers said a further drop of yields on secondary markets could be difficult.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think that yields could fall significantly further," a trader said. "Much stronger (investor) confidence would be needed for that, with the forint firmer than 280 or even near 275."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                           change   change\par                                           today    in 2010 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   24.516    24.626  +0.45%  +7.35%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>   3.925    3.931  +0.15%   +4.56%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>   281.34    282.98  +0.58%  -3.91%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>   7.28    7.283  +0.04%   +0.4%\par Romanian leu     <EURRON=>   4.231    4.259  +0.66%   +0.15%\par Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>   105.19    105.12   -0.07%    -8.85%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +3 basis points to  103bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    -3 basis points to  +94bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +97bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds <0#HUBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +591bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +553bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR +3 basis points to  +462bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent. All data taken from Reuters at 1551 CET. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Curre