\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Romania economy doesn't justify higher leu - cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerned about leu strength hurting economy\par \par \uc2 * Could continue \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent strong rise\par \par \uc2 * Leu hits weakest level in nearly three weeks <EURRON=>\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment, updated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move)\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, March 31 (Reuters) - Romania's current economic fundamentals do not justify further firming of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Cristian Popa was quoted as saying on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The national bank has previously expressed concern the leu, which hit its strongest level since January 2009 earlier this month, could firm too much towards levels that could hurt exporters and hamper economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has benefited from improved sentiment among foreign investors and the country's lower risk profile after it revived an International Monetary Fund-led aid deal. It is now up 3.5 percent on the year.\par \par \uc2 "Economic fundamentals right now do not justify a stronger leu appreciation," Popa was quoted as saying by daily Ziarul Financiar.\par \par \uc2 The leu fell after Popa's comments and was down 0.7 percent compared with Tuesday's close at 4.095 per euro at 0935 GMT, its weakest level in nearly three weeks.\par \par \uc2 Popa's statement "sounds like a verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to us and will not help the leu to regain bullish momentum," 4Cast analyst Piotr Matys said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "At least Easter remittances are still offering the leu some support and should prevent EUR/RON from gaining upside traction with gains capped below 4.10."\par \par \uc2 Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly in the market last week to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it hit 14-month highs. [ID:nLDE62P0OO]\par \par \uc2 The leu has since fallen back, pressured by a cut in interest rates and market expectations of further easing to come after Popa revealed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate decision had been unanimous. [ID:nLDE62T0WF]\par \par \uc2 "We read this as a sign supporting our updated call for another 50bp cut at the upcoming meeting, since unanimity could mean there is little reason to ease the pace of cuts at this point," said ING economist Vlad Muscalu. (Reporting by Luiza Ilie and Sam Cage; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA-LEU/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RDN|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100331e63v000e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
