\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-C.Europe to fight  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains with  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , low rates\b0\par\par\uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Further \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains to reduce chances for economic recovery\par \par \uc2 * Central banks talk down \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to staunch firming\par \par \uc2 * Markets may turn more dovish on interest rates\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/310/EZ_CEEFX0310.gif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/310/EZ_CEEFX0310.gif }}}\par \par \uc2 (Adds graph of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Marius Zaharia\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, March 10 (Reuters) - The rebound in the EU's emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may hurt economic recovery this year and policymakers look set to fend off investors by keeping interest rates low and threatening market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Poland, the Czech Republic, Hungary and Romania are still well below pre-crisis highs, weak demand for the region's exports in the euro zone has officials worrying that excessive strength could hurt growth.\par \par \uc2 Drawn by a solid economic outlook, investors propelled the zloty and the crown to 15-month and four-month peaks this week, while the forint and leu have been helped by their official interest rates of 5.75 and 7 percent.\par \par \uc2 The zloty surge, a 23 percent gain in 13 months, has prompted two ministers to talk down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month and central bankers there have cast doubt on the timing of rate hikes that would raise the zloty's allure. [ID:nLDE6281MH]\par \par \uc2 For a graph of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in the region, click on: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/310/EZ_CEEFX0310.gif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/310/EZ_CEEFX0310.gif }}}\par \par \uc2 Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor also signalled last week he was concerned the leu could firm too far, spreading fear among dealers that the bank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 4 and 4.1 lei per euro, virtually freezing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nLDE62313Q]\par \par \uc2 "We are at a stage where they are afraid that their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are going too strong," said Gyula Toth, EMEA economist and strategist at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  in Vienna.\par \par \uc2 "You have a situation when there is a constant inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the country, and from this perspective they will have to fight quite heavily (against \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  firming.)"\par \par \uc2 UNDESIRED FIRMING\par \par \uc2 Analysts think Poland and Czech Republic will hike rates twice in the second half of the year, and markets expect Romania to cut by one percentage point in 2010 and Hungary by 25-75 basis points, depending on developments after an April election.\par \par \uc2 But according to a Reuters poll <CEEFXPOLL01>, all of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to appreciate this year.\par \par \uc2 Even turmoil tied to debt-stricken Greece is seen helping, as it has pushed some investors away from troubled euro zone periphery states into more solid-looking economies further east.\par \par \uc2 Polish Deputy Prime Minister Waldemar Pawlak said a zloty level of around 4.0 per euro was desirable, a statement bringing to mind the government's forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last year when it tried to keep the zloty from weakening by converting European Union development funds.\par \par \uc2 The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against crown firming last year and analysts said they could do so again if the unit approached 25 per euro. [ID:nL58899]\par \par \uc2 "In \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  there was already a hint the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the Czech Republic... we saw verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year and those might come back, and in Hungary it is already possible to see verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Elisabeth Gruie, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 She believes markets are pricing in excessively high levels for rates and sees no hikes in the region this year, a thought echoed by others.\par \par \uc2 "Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the end will tend to delay rate hikes," said Timothy Ash, an analyst with RBS in London.\par \par \uc2 INVESTMENT FLOWS\par \par \uc2 Raising rates would attract more flows into straight \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays. Otherwise, if investors are not going to get more gains from \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they may switch more focus to debt and equities trades.\par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  sees more flows into regional debt than \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  instruments in the short term, and \uc2 Barclays\uc2  is especially upbeat on Romanian bonds, as rates have more room to fall there and the country is pursuing budget cuts backed by the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 Low \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility would also redirect flows to other emerging markets such as Asia or Latin America, which are more tolerant to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2 If growth does stay strong, governments may also have more political room to carry out further fiscal reforms, although elections this year across the region may prove a bigger barrier to any such tightening of public purse strings.\par \par \uc2 Locking in a competitive advantage against euro zone countries and shoring up growth will also benefit incumbent administrations.\par \par \uc2 "If you're looking for a soft patch and not a double dip recession, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength already starts to become an issue," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 's Gruie. (Editing by Michael Winfrey and Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 EASTEUROPE-RECOVERY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS, PIX)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|PX|CZS|RDN|GNN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100310e63a0011j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
