\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Nov 2\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2009\par 08:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Nov 2 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Monday.\par \par \uc2 IMF MISSION VISIT\par \par \uc2 An IMF mission is in Bucharest to review Romania's progress in meeting conditions of a 20 billion euros aid package.\par \par \uc2 DEBT AUCTION\par \par \uc2 Romania's finance ministry tenders 1.2 billion lei ($410.7 million) in six-month treasury bills.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA'S LEFTISTS TO BACK IMF-MANDATED 2010 BUDGET\par \par \uc2 Romania's powerful leftist opposition will back a speedy parliamentary approval of the 2010 budget to help Bucharest get a much needed IMF loan tranche and unlock a policy freeze ahead of a Nov. 22 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLU224925]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN LEU FIRMS, DEALERS CITE CBANK\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu bucked the regional trend and firmed around half a percent on Friday, moving off its lowest level since February with dealers citing covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLU587193]\par \par \uc2 2010 BUDGET\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  must have a voted 2010 budget by Dec. 10 so that it can receive the third IMF loan tranche, Romania's representative to the IMF Mihai Tanasescu was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 2\par \par \uc2 ROMGAZ\par \par \uc2 Romania's state-owned gas company Romgaz posted a 5 percent drop in its nine-month net profit to 419.8 million lei ($144.4 million).\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 20\par \par \uc2 REACTORS 3 AND 4\par \par \uc2 State-owned nuclear power plant operator Nuclearelectrica will not be able to retain a 51 percent participation in the future reactors 3 and 4, an investment estimated at about 4 billion euros, deputy Economy Minister Tudor Serban said.\par \par \uc2 He said private investors' participation could be bigger that originally decided.\par \par \uc2 ENERGY PRICES\par \par \uc2 Gas and electricity prices will not be hiked in 2010, acting prime minister Emil Boc said.\par \par \uc2 Romania Libera, Page 7\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|RDN|REVU|G|RBN|GNN|ABN|E|U|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCO|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091102e5b2000kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
