\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on March 26\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, March 26 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  CONFERENCE\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Mugur Isarescu holds news conference on the 20 billion euro IMF-led financial package for Romania. Event starts at 1000 GMT.\par \par \uc2 FINMIN\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Gheorghe Pogea is expected to attend a financial seminar to discuss fiscal code proposed amendments with private companies.\par \par \uc2 Romania secures 20 bln euro IMF-led rescue\par \par \uc2 Romania has secured a 20 billion euro aid package from the International Monetary Fund and the European Union in a bid to thwart a financing crisis and stabilise its stricken economy.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLP226693]\par \par \uc2 IMF to urge Western banks to keep Romanian exposure\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund said it would ask top Western banks operating in Romania to affirm support for local subsidiaries and back an IMF-led rescue package by keeping their exposure to the struggling EU member.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLP957960]\par \par \uc2 IMF SAYS DOESN'T RULE OUT ROMANIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund said on Wednesday the Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will not change as a result of an aid package given to the new European Union member.\par \par \uc2 The Fund's chief of mission to \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  said this meant some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be ruled out.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLP228254]\par \par \uc2 Romania faces stiff test despite IMF leniency\par \par \uc2 Romania may have gained some leniency from the International Monetary Fund and the European Union in a 20 billion euro aid package, but the long-term fiscal reforms demanded by the lenders may well founder, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLP317888]\par \par \uc2 UNION PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 Cartel Alfa and the railroad union representatives announced plans to stage nationwide protests if the government will not hike their wages and implement a tough restructuring programme requiring mass layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, page 2\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN WORKERS FROM ABROAD\par \par \uc2 The labour ministry expects up to 300,000 Romanians workers to return mainly from Spain and Italy as they lose jobs due to the economic crisis. Because of this, the ministry could revise unemployment forecast for 2009.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, page 2\par \par \uc2 TRANSGAZ INVESTMENTS\par \par \uc2 State-controlled gas pipeline operator Transgaz will invest 100 million euros in 2009 in new and already begun projects, 25 percent more than in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, page 11\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   