\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on March 3\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 08:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, March 3 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA HOLDS PRELIMINARY TALKS WITH IMF-SOURCE\par \par \uc2 Romania has started preliminary discussions with the IMF on an aid deal to help patch up finances strained by global crisis and calm nervous markets, a source close to the talks said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL2546484]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA STICKS TO 2014 EURO ENTRY GOAL-REPORT\par \par \uc2 Romania's centre-left government has kept its 2014 deadline for joining the euro in a convergence report sent to Brussels, hoping it will give it enough time to enforce much needed reforms.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL2125059]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  CBANK \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES FALL, SUGGESTING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, excluding 103.7 tonnes of gold, fell by 92 million euros ($116 million) to 25.9 billion euros in February, signalling possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the leu.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL2381050]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  SELLS 2.52 BLN LEI IN 6-MO TBILLS\par \par \uc2 Romania sold 2.52 billion lei ($736.6 million) in 6-month treasury bills on Monday, with the average accepted yield at 11.48 percent, from 11.46 percent at a previous tender of Feb. 2, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nBUC001288]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA BANK DISADVANTAGED BY FOREIGN AID\par \par \uc2 Banca Transilvania\uc2 , Romania's top locally-owned lender, on Monday called on the government to guarantee banks' funding in euros to help them compete with foreign-held banks that have benefited from state aid.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL2167068]\par \par \uc2 ENERGY PRICES\par \par \uc2 Energy tariffs could rise this year due to a drop in consumption, which would mean fewer consumers would have to handle fixed industry costs, Romania's power grid operator \uc2 Transelectrica\uc2  estimated on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Evenimentul Zilei, Page 10\par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 The Democrat-Liberals, part of the ruling centre-left coalition, decided on Monday that party members who already hold public offices will not be on the candidates' list for European Parliament election due later this year.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, Page 6\par \par \uc2 TREASON CHARGES\par \par \uc2 Romanian prosecutors said on Monday they got arrest warrants for a Romanian officer and a Bulgarian citizen on charges of treason and espionage.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, Page 3\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters