\par\par \b \uc2 Romania leu bucks regional weakness, mkt cites cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2009\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Romania's leu bucked the regional weakening trend on Friday and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helped by the Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint <EURHUF=> fell 2.2 percent, the Polish zloty <EURPLN=> dropped 1.8 percent and the Czech crown <EURCZK=> weakened by 1.3 percent, while the leu <EURRON=> firmed 0.6 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold euros through commercial banks to bring the leu from 4.34 to 4.29 per euro," one dealer with a local bank said. "It heavily sold euros between 1200 and 1300 (1000-1100 GMT) and it sold some more at different times throughout the day."\par \par \uc2 Over the last several months, dealers have suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally as economic concerns and uncertainty over fiscal policies following November's parliamentary election weighed on the leu.\par \par \uc2 Piraeus bank analysts wrote in an afternoon note that Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the most consistent from the start of the year and it was aimed at defending the 4.35 level.\par \par \uc2 "It sold 300-400 million euros," a dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest said. The leu has been one of the most battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in eastern Europe this year, hitting successive record lows against the euro last week as investors feared financing risks stemming from Romania's vast budget and current account deficits.\par \par \uc2 Romania is seen as one of the most risky economies in emerging Europe in the wake of the global financial crisis, and is the only European Union country rated below investment grade by some rating agencies.\par \par \uc2 At 1255 GMT, the leu <EURRON=> traded at 4.3050 per euro, compared with an intra-day low of 4.3405 per euro and a high of 4.2920. Last week it hit a record low of 4.3530.\par \par \uc2 The bank has admitted to only a small amount of leu-buying in October as the financial crisis pummelled global markets. (Reporting by Marius Zaharia, Editing by David Stamp)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -LEU/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090123e51n001ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
