\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Jan 14\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2009\par 08:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Jan 14 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 T-BILLS\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions off 800 million lei worth of 91-day treasury bills.\par \par \uc2 EASTEUROPE INFLATION\par \par \uc2 December inflation slowed faster than expected in Slovakia, Bulgaria and Romania, pointing to rate cuts in the latter and showing price pressures weakening across the EU's eastern members as a global slowdown takes hold.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLD714175]\par \par \uc2 INTERIOR MINISTER RESIGNATION\par \par \uc2 Romania's new government suffered a blow on Tuesday with the resignation of Interior Minister Gabriel Oprea, embroiled in a row with coalition partners over appointment of an intelligence chief.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLD354760]\par \par \uc2 BCR STRIKE\par \par \uc2 Employees of Romania's biggest bank BCR postponed a pay strike planned for Wednesday after receiving a new pay offer, the head of the bank's staff union said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLD145507]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  LEU FIRMS VS EURO, DEALERS CITE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leu regained some ground against the euro on Tuesday after falling nearly 1 percent to hit an all-time low earlier in the session, with dealers citing covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLD353441]\par \par \uc2 BUDGET BILL\par \par \uc2 The government will have a first reading of the budget draft on Friday, and the bill will be sent to parliament on Jan. 24 for approval, Economy Minister Adriean Videanu said.\par \par \uc2 DACIA\par \par \uc2 Romanian carmaker Dacia, owned by France's Renault , may oust up to 4,000 people in the coming months if the global financial crisis deepens, the company said on Tuesday after the protest organized by the workers union.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, page 6\par \par \uc2 PLANS TO FIGHT CRISIS\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Gheorghe Pogea said the government's plan to combat the effects of the global cash shortage will be released after Jan, 22 after consultations with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trade unions and employers.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, page 9\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|RDN|REVU|G|RBN|GNN|ABN|E|U|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCO|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090114e51e000f5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
