\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-C.bank boosts Romania's leu; IMF lifts forint\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jason Hovet  \par \uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2009\par 16:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout)\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The Romanian leu recovered strongly on Tuesday as dealers cited \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Hungarian forint also jumped, helped by IMF assurances Hungary was on track with its $25 billion aid package.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded after nearing new lows in earlier trade, which helped erase losses in emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite persistent concerns about the region's economies.\par \par \uc2 Mounting evidence the global economic slowdown will take a heavy toll on emerging Europe and falling risk appetite have hung on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past week, renewing a weakening trend started in the second half of 2008. A dragging Russia-Ukraine gas row has also added to concern. [ID:nLD708539]\par \par \uc2 Dealers cited \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helping lift the leu <EURRON=> 1.9 percent to 4.233 per euro. It was the first sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since December. [ID:LD353441]\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, the forint was up 1.8 percent from Monday's domestic close at 276.5 per euro by 1507 GMT, which pushed bond yields down. Earlier, the forint closed in on the 286 level, last hit in October when the escalating financial crisis battered central Europe.\par \par \uc2 The forint had fallen sharply in the past few days due in part to market speculation the IMF would scold Hungary over a lack of progress on the terms of an aid deal struck in October to allay external financing concerns.\par \par \uc2 But in Budapest on Tuesday, the fund's head Dominique Strauss-Kahn said Hungary was making progress. [ID:nLD334802]\par \par \uc2 "(The 286 level) might be hard to break from a technical standpoint. Both of these facts together have created a correction in the forint," said Ulrich Leuchtmann, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research as \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in Frankfurt, referring also to IMF comments.\par \par \uc2 CONTAGION\par \par \uc2 The leu and forint remained down 5.2 percent and 4.7 percent respectively in 2009. Analysts have said Romania, with a large current account deficit, may need its own aid package to restore confidence.\par \par \uc2 "Investors have lost confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one Bucharest dealer said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness and nagging inflation have limited the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's scope for joining the regional trend of cutting rates to counter collapsing demand for the area's exports.\par \par \uc2 Data on Tuesday showing Romania's annual inflation rate eased to 6.3 percent in December from 6.7 percent may lift some concerns. [ID:nLD37336]\par \par \uc2 In other trade, the Czech crown <EURCZK=> edged up to 26.63 per euro. Poland's zloty led losses with a 0.7 percent drop to 4.12 the euro, and more weakness was expected.\par \par \uc2 "We see high probability of a weaker zloty because economic conditions are deteriorating fast, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to use non-conventional measures to support the financial system, which may have a negative impact on the zloty," said Shahin Vallee, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Serbian dinar <EURRSD=>, which has also hit new lows in the past week, was up 0.5 percent at 91.87 per euro in choppy trade, helped by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale of 12 million euros.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2009 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   26.633   26.7    +0.25%   +0.45%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    4.118    4.089  -0.7%    -0.07%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  276.47   281.31   +1.75%   -4.67%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>    7.33     7.339  +0.12%   +0.48%\par Romanian leu     <EURRON=>    4.233    4.315  +1.94%   -5.16%\par Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>   91.87    92.341  +0.51%   -2.6%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    -3 basis points to  142bps over bmk*\par 4-yr T-bond   CZ4YT=RR    -9 basis points to  +135bps over bmk*\par 8-yr T-bond   CZ8YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +117bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds <0#PLBMK=>\par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +330bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR    -1 basis points to  +274bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR    -3 basis points to  +233bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds <0#HUBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR    -15 basis points to  +826bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR    -21 basis points to  +794bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR  -28 basis points to  +612bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent. All data taken from Reuters at 1610 CET. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic close at 1600 GMT. For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets