\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Dec 16\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2008\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 COALITION TALKS\par \par \uc2 Romanian Democrat-Liberals and Social Democrats, who have forged a governing coalition, meet to discuss the structure of the upcoming government.\par \par \uc2 * The future government may have 7 ministers and one deputy prime minister more than the current structure, according to papers related to the coalition's regulations.\par \par \uc2 Romania Libera, Page 5\par \par \uc2 BOC WINS ROMANIA PM NOMINATION AS DEPUTY STANDS DOWN\par \par \uc2 The head of Romania's Democrat-Liberal (PD-L) party Emil Boc won the mandate to form a centre-left government on Monday after his deputy declined the nomination, fuelling fears of political rifts and instability.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLF674105]\par \par \uc2 * For a factbox of five facts about the Romanian prime minister designate please double click on [ID:nLF398317].\par \par \uc2 * For an instant view, please double-click on [ID:nLF70292].\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA Q3 FINAL CONSUMPTION SPEEDS UP TO 13.7 PCT\par \par \uc2 Romania's final consumption growth accelerated to 13.7 percent in the third quarter from 9 percent in the same period of 2007, powered by rampant domestic spending, National Statistics Board data showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLF677145]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA BUDGET REVENUES UP 26.8 PCT Y/Y IN JAN-NOV\par \par \uc2 Romania's budget revenues rose to 139.08 billion lei ($47.6 billion) in the first 11 months of the year, up 26.8 percent from the same period last year, data from the finance and economy ministry showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLF689109]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN LEU JUMPS, DEALERS SUSPECT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Romanian leu jumped sharply against the euro on Monday, rebounding from a two-month low, with dealers saying they suspected indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLF717213]\par \par \uc2 COALITION OFFICIAL SAYS \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  NEEDS IMF DEAL\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  should seek financing from the International Monetary Fund to shore up its finances and limit the economic downturn, according to a senior strategist from the centre-left coalition likely to form the next government.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLF695083]\par \par \uc2 FINMIN DEBT\par \par \uc2 The finance and economy ministry borrowed 1.9 billion lei ($650.7 million) in 8-day deposits on the interbank market, at an average accepted yield of 13.45 percent.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 6\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN TROOPS IN IRAQ\par \par \uc2 The Iraqi government will vote on Tuesday on a proposal to ask Romanian troops to remain in the country in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Cotidianul, Page 8\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]