\par\par \b \uc2 TRADE IDEA-Erste recommends closing euro/Romanian leu short\b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2008\par 13:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Oct 17 (Reuters) - Erste bank recommended on Friday investors close short positions in the euro against the leu at 3.72 per euro, saying the Romanian unit has little room to firm because global financial woes enhanced worries over external vulnerabilities.\par \par \uc2 Romania is seen as one of the most vulnerable countries in the region because of its vast current account deficit and its high proportion of hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lending, coupled with lax fiscal and income policies.\par \par \uc2 "There is a low probability of further recovery of the leu amid gloomy global context," Erste said in a report.\par \par \uc2 "The deepening of the global financial crisis, coupled with the lax fiscal policy ... determined a sharp depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro ... The fall of the leu could only be halted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and brought the exchange rate below 3.75 per euro."\par \par \uc2 The leu reached its lowest level in almost four years at 3.9860 per euro <EURRON=> on Oct. 6, but regained some of its losses in recent days as dealers cited several covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Marius Zaharia; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -LEU/TRADE|LANGEN|RDN|GNN|ABN|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081020e4ah0010o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
