\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Oct 13\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2008\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Oct 13 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Monday.\par \par \uc2 CURRENT ACCOUNT\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to release Jan-Aug current account data.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  CBANK SAYS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENED\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO TEST MARKET\par \par \uc2 The Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the leu on Friday, directly selling 40 million euros ($55 million) in a move it said was primarily aimed at testing the market.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLA347531]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN PRICE GROWTH EASES, SLOVAK AT 4-YR HIGH\par \par \uc2 Inflation in Romania slowed less than forecast in September and hit an almost four-year high in Slovakia, and analysts said it would still take time to further loosen the clamps on monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLA726651]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA JAN-AUG TRADE DEFICIT UP 9.4 PCT Y/Y\par \par \uc2 Romania's January-August trade deficit widened by 9.4 percent on the year to 14.6 billion euros ($20.04 billion), data from the National Statistics Board (INS) showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nBUC001053]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA CBANK SAYS TESTED \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MKT AT 1300 GMT\par \par \uc2 The Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had tested the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at 1300 GMT but made no transactions. Dealers said earlier that the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time on Friday at around that hour.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLA273007]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN PRESIDENT URGES WAGE CAUTION IN CRISIS\par \par \uc2 Romanian President Traian Basescu urged on Friday for the government, parliament and trade unions, clashing over wage claims in the run up to the Nov. 30 election, to minimise the impact of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLA583771]\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST BOURSE\par \par \uc2 The Bucharest Stock Exchange halted trade on Friday as global markets tumbled to new lows in a panic sell-off.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nLA168485]\par \par \uc2 ALLIANCES\par \par \uc2 * The ruling Liberal party of Prime Minister Calin Tariceanu will most probably govern with leftist opposition Social Democrat Party after the Nov. 30 parliamentary election, said Liberal vice-president Crin Antonescu.\par \par \uc2 Romania libera, page 6\par \par \uc2 * Romania's centrist opposition leader Theodor Stolojan, the Democrat-Liberal Party's candidate for prime-minister, said he preffers a collaboration with the Liberals, but only if they get rid of Tariceanu.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 26\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  -------------