\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on Oct 7\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2008\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 PAY PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 Trade unionists from various sectors hold rally in downtown Bucharest to ask for wage increases after parliament approval of a hefty 50 percent pay increase only for teachers last week.\par \par \uc2 INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT\par \par \uc2 The National Statistics Board to release August industrial output data.\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA BANKS SAFE FROM CRISIS, C.BANK MONITORING\par \par \uc2 Romania's banking system is safe from the world crisis and has excess liquidity but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was committed to inject funds if needed to ensure financial stability, governor Mugur Isarescu said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL6119906]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA CBANK SEEN STEPPING IN INDIRECTLY TO SLOW LEU FALL\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by indirectly selling euros to prop up the leu <EURRON=>, dealers said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL6295308]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN NET WAGES UP 24 PCT Y/Y IN AUGUST\par \par \uc2 Romania's average net wages rose 24 percent on the year in nominal terms in August to 1,277 lei ($440), and were down 2.4 percent from July, data from the National Statistics Board (INS) showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 [ID:nL6241833]\par \par \uc2 PARLIAMENT ACTIVITY\par \par \uc2 The speaker of parliament's lower chamber Bogdan Olteanu said he could suspend parliament activity until the Nov. 30 election, unless parties reach an agreement to stop passing bills which could hamper Romania's financial stability.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the parliament approved a 50 percent hike in teachers' wages, a move that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government described as unsustainable and damaging for the overheated economy.\par \par \uc2 Gandul, page 5\par \par \uc2 SOCIAL-DEMOCRATS DEMAND C.BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The leader of \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's opposition Social-Democrat Party Mircea Geoana asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop a fall in the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 2\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|RDN|REVU|G|RBN|GNN|ABN|E|U|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCO|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA00000200810