\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on July 15\b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2008\par 08:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, July 15 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 CURRENT ACCOUNT\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may release January-May current account deficit figures.\par \par \uc2 BUDGET REVISION\par \par \uc2 Romania will allocate 2.3 billion lei ($973.8 million) for infrastructure projects, 200 million lei for defence acquisitions and 376 million lei for social spending in a budget revision expected to be approved by the government this week, Ziarul Financiar quotes official sources as saying.\par \par \uc2 The government is expected to keep the budget deficit unchanged at 2.3 percent of the gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 3\par \par \uc2 LEU PROSPECTS\par \par \uc2 Investors should not bet on an appreciation of the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond 3.4 per euro <EURRON=> as \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weak economic fundamentals and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter a steep rise.\par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, page 1\par \par \uc2 MORTGAGES PLANS\par \par \uc2 One out of ten Romanians plans to buy a house in the next three years, a study by \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  group showed. It estimates mortgage loans will rise by 40 percent by 2010.\par \par \uc2 Gandul, page 7\par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].\par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -----------------------------------------