\par\par \b \uc2 Romania leu at one-week highs on cbank comments   \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2008\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Jan 17 (Reuters) - The Romanian leu retraced this week's losses to reach a one week high against the euro on Thursday, helped by recent comments by central bankers that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still attractive, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Cristian Popa said the leu's fall to almost three-year lows this week had gone too far, while an adviser of the bank's governor said the leu remained attractive after a recent interest rate hike.   \par \par \uc2 After hitting a near five-year high versus the euro last summer, the leu has been emerging Europe's punch bag because of Romania's current account gap of around 14 percent of GDP and the absence of a policy response to it.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  made \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2  look more positive for now, showed some unhappiness in Bucharest about the weak leu and this is a good sign," said one dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest.   \par \par \uc2 "But the current account is still huge so the leu will not firm too much for too long."   \par \par \uc2 By 0830 GMT the leu firmed to as much as 3.6570 per euro <EURRON=> compared with Wednesday's close of 3.6825 and a near three year low of 3.7240 on Monday. --------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0830 GMT ---------------- Leu/euro <EURRON=> at 3.6617 bid vs 3.6825 on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Leu/dollar <RON=>  at 2.5101 bid vs 2.5198.\par  -------------RELATED NEWS (double click to access) ---------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight