\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Romania \highlight\uc2  has option to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  market-cbanker   \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2008\par 10:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Jan 16 (Reuters) - The Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated on Wednesday its policy to reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and said such moves would not be announced in advance.   \par \par \uc2  The bank's chief economist Valentin Lazea said economic problems such as a vast trade deficit differentiated Romania from its eastern European neighbours and were behind a recent decline in the leu \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to three-year lows versus the euro.   \par \par \uc2  "The bank operates with the interest rate first of all," Lazea was quoted as saying by Rompres news agency.   \par \par \uc2  "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it is keeping the option to use other instruments, if need be, including direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, except that, of course, they will not be announced in advance."   \par \par \uc2  The leu has been emerging Europe's punching bag since hitting an almost five-year high against the euro in the summer of 2007. It hit a near three-year low of 3.7240 <EURRON=> earlier this week on worries about economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, it traded at 3.7020 per euro.   \par \par \uc2  The Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially since September 2005 when it moved to weaken the leu. The bank has declined to comment on rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since. Traders have said they suspected covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of lei late last year when the leu was falling sharply in November.   \par \par \uc2  "We must start from the fact that the recent leu fall ... isn't reflected in other central European countries," Lazea said.   \par \par \uc2  "This means Romania has a certain problem ... the foreign deficit ... which in turn reflects a more structural problem. Economic growth in Romania is based particularly on consumption, whereas in central European countries it is based both on consumption and exports."   \par \par \uc2  Voracious demand last year, Romania's first in the EU, has bloated the current account deficit to an expected 14 percent of gross domestic product and has pushed inflation to 6.6 percent in December, well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 3-5 percent target.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its benchmark rate 50 basis points to 8 percent earlier this month and analysts widely expect it to continue the tightening cycle when it meets next in February.  (Reporting by Luiza Ilie; Editing by Stephen Nisbet)     \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA-CBANK/LEU|LANGEN|RDN|GNN|ABN|M|D|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080116e41g000ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
