\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on September 6   \b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2007\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 6 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 EC HEAD MEETS ROMANIAN OFFICIALS   \par \par \uc2 President of the European Commission Jose Manuel Barroso meets Romanian officials in Sibiu and Bucharest on a two-day visit to the new EU member.   \par \par \uc2 FINMIN NEWS CONFERENCE   \par \par \uc2 Finance and Economy Minister Varujan Vosganian holds a news conference on energy and fiscal policy issues.   \par \par \uc2 10-YEAR BOND TENDER   \par \par \uc2 The Finance and Economy Ministry is expected to launch a tender for 100 million lei worth of 10-year T-bonds.   \par \par \uc2 OIL SEMINAR   \par \par \uc2 Finance and Economy Minister Varujan Vosganian and representatives of top regional oil and gas firms are expected to attend a two-day seminar.   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA GOVT APPROVES ENERGY SECTOR REVAMP   \par \par \uc2 Romania's government cleared on Wednesday a long-term energy strategy which sets up an integrated electricity holding and envisions investment in the sector of about 35 billion euros ($48 billion).   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05914218]   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN FINMIN SEES 2007 GDP GROWTH AT 6-6.5 PCT   \par \par \uc2 Romania's Finance Minister Varujan Vosganian on Wednesday said he was optimistic the economy will grow 6 to 6.5 percent this year.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nBUC000799]   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIAN PM SAYS FORD DEAL TO BE COMPLETED SOON   \par \par \uc2 Romanian Prime Minister Calin Tariceanu said on Wednesday he was optimistic his cabinet will soon seal a deal to sell troubled carmaker  \uc2 Automobile Craiova SA\uc2  to U.S. firm  \uc2 Ford Motor Co\uc2  .   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05889806]   \par \par \uc2 CANADIAN GOLD MINER DEFENDS CYANIDE USE IN ROMANIA   \par \par \uc2 A Canadian miner, which wants to set up Europe's biggest goldmine in Romania, defended plans on Wednesday to use cyanide to extract gold and criticised Hungary for trying to block the project.   \par \par \uc2 [ID:nL05137139]   \par \par \uc2 ROMANIA LEU EXTENDS LOSS TO 4-MONTH LOW VS EURO   \par \par \uc2 Romania's leu <EURRON=> fell further against the euro on Wednesday, hitting its lowest level in more than four months as investors worried about economic fundamentals and potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 [ID:L0513618]   \par \par \uc2 CARREFOUR \b \highlight22\uc2 ROMANIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  IMPORTS UP 25 PCT IN H1   \par \par \uc2 The Romanian unit of retailer Carrefour saw its imports rise by 25 percent since Romania joined the European Union in January.   \par \par \uc2 Ziarul Financiar, Page 7   \par \par \uc2 NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2 For other related news, double click on:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 L