\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to Watch on September 4   \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2007\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BUCHAREST, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  GDP DATA   \par \par \uc2  The National Statistics Board will release second quarter gross domestic product data at 0700 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  ROMANIAN DIPLOMACY MEETING   \par \par \uc2  Foreign ministers from France, Britain and Serbia, Bernard Kouchner, David Miliband and Vuk Jeremic, attend \b \highlight22\uc2 Romania\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual diplomacy reunion.   \par \par \uc2  AUG \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES UP, RAISE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  TALK   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday a steep rise in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in August, signalling that the bank may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the leu last month, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL03748896]   \par \par \uc2  AVERAGE NET WAGES UP 23.5 PCT Y/Y IN JULY   \par \par \uc2  Romania's average net wages jumped 23.5 percent on the year in nominal terms in July to 1,040 lei ($435), boosted by bonuses, salary negotiations and higher industrial production, statistical data showed on Monday.   \par \par \uc2  [ID:nL03562417]   \par \par \uc2  FUEL SUPPLY COSTS UP 4.2 PCT Y/Y   \par \par \uc2  Fuel supply costs in the economy are estimated to reach 4.32 billion lei ($1.80 billion) between Oct. 1 and March 31, 2008, a 4.2 percent year on year rise.   \par \par \uc2  Gandul, page 9   \par \par \uc2  FORD PRODUCTION   \par \par \uc2 Ford Motor Co\uc2   may start car production at the Craiova-based Automobile SA plant as early as 12-15 weeks after signing a deal to acquire the troubled carmaker from the Romanian government.   \par \par \uc2  Ziarul Financiar, page 3   \par \par \uc2  ELECTORAL REFORM   \par \par \uc2  A law to change the current electoral system to allow voters cast ballots for individuals is likely to be approved by the end of October, Senate head Nicolae Vacaroiu was quoted as saying.   \par \par \uc2  Evenimentul Zilei, page 7   \par \par \uc2  NOTE - For a diary of forthcoming Romanian events, double click [RO/DIARY], and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see [CONV/DIARY].   \par \par \uc2  For other related news, double click on:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romania Market Debt     [RO-DBT]   Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [RO-FRX]\par  Romania Market Report   [ROL/]     Romanian money      [RO-M]\par  Emerging Market Debt    [EMRG/DBT] Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [EMRG/FRX]\par  All Emerging Markets news [EMRG]   CEE indicators  [CONV/DIARY]\par  All East Europe News       [EEU]   E.Europe equities     [.CEE]\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets   [TOP/EMRG]\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch  [TOP/EAST]\par  Romanian indicators        [RO/ECI]\par  Main page of Reuters poll  <RO/POLL1>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|RDN|REVU|G|RBN|GNN|RNP|DNP|PGE|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070904e394000bl\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\as